      "description": "Search Page Home Explore JMU Benefits Navigate JMU Job Search My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode Skip to jobs search results Category Search categories 19 filter options found Category Administrative / Office Staff (5 items) 5 Advancement (5 items) 5 Athletics (4 items) 4 Budget / Finance / Payroll (2 items) 2 Communications / Marketing (1 items) 1 Director / Unit Head (2 items) 2 Facilities / Skilled Trades (12 items) 12 Fundraising / Philanthropy (4 items) 4 Graduate Assistant (1 items) 1 Health Center (3 items) 3 Housekeeping (7 items) 7 Human resources (1 items) 1 Information Technology (1 items) 1 Instructional / Teaching Faculty (8 items) 8 Libraries (1 items) 1 Other (13 items) 13 Police Department (1 items) 1 Research (1 items) 1 Student Employment (25 items) 25 Department Search departments 32 filter options found Department Academic Affairs Unit (2 items) 2 Access and Enrollment (1 items) 1 Admissions (1 items) 1 Advancement Information Services (2 items) 2 Advancement Marketing (1 items) 1 Business Services (22 items) 22 Center for Global Engagement (1 items) 1 College of Arts and Letters (2 items) 2 College of Business (3 items) 3 College of Education (2 items) 2 College of Health and Behavioral Studies (9 items) 9 College of Science and Mathematics (5 items) 5 College of Visual and Performing Arts (2 items) 2 Constituent Engagement and Sustained Giving (3 items) 3 Development (3 items) 3 Finance (1 items) 1 Financial Aid and Scholarships (1 items) 1 Health and Wellbeing (3 items) 3 Human Resources, Training and Performance (4 items) 4 Information Technology (1 items) 1 Intercollegiate Athletics (5 items) 5 JMU Libraries (1 items) 1 Office of the President Unit (1 items) 1 Police and Public Safety (2 items) 2 Principal Relationships (1 items) 1 School of Professional & Continuing Education (1 items) 1 Student Academic Success (1 items) 1 Student Access and Inclusion (2 items) 2 Student Life and Involvement (2 items) 2 The Graduate School (1 items) 1 University Studies (1 items) 1 Vice President - REDI (2 items) 2 Employment Type Search employment types 9 filter options found Employment Type Adjunct Faculty (2 items) 2 Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) (12 items) 12 Federal Work Study (10 items) 10 Full-time Staff (Classified) (32 items) 32 Graduate Assistant (1 items) 1 Institutional Employment (15 items) 15 Instructional / Teaching Faculty (6 items) 6 Part-time - Wage / Part-time Salaried (11 items) 11 Temporary (1 items) 1 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Sort by: Last Updated Last Updated: Newest to Oldest Last Updated: Oldest to Newest Title: A-Z Title: Z-A Registered Dietitian - 9-Month Position 20002254 Harrisonburg, Virginia Health and Wellbeing Health Center Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) The University Health Center provides a comprehensive array of health care services and health education programs to JMU students. Included in our health care services are several medical and specialty clinics, a pharmacy, a medical laboratory, and other collaborative programs that provide services for more than 30,000 patient encounters a year. UHC practices evidence-based medicine in a confidential, inclusive environment.\n\nThe Registered Dietitian Nutritionist role within the UHC offers an opportunity not only to provide on-going nutrition counseling and education to JMU students both 1:1 and in group settings, but to collaborate with multidisciplinary teams for quality care and to mentor nutrition students/volunteers that are vital to nutrition clinic operations.\" Read more IT Policy and Compliance Analyst 20002264 Harrisonburg, Virginia Information Technology Information Technology Full-time Staff (Classified) James Madison University is accepting applications for an Information Technology Policy and Compliance Analyst to provide support for Information Technology's Third-Party Vendor Management Program. The successful candidate will assist IT in ensuring compliance with applicable information technology regulations, policies, and standards.\n\nThis position is eligible for a hybrid work schedule. Read more Student Assistant - FWS 20002258 Harrisonburg, Virginia The Graduate School Student Employment Federal Work Study Closing on: Sep 18 2026 The Graduate School (TGS) is accepting applications for Graduate School Student Assistant who will be responsible for offering support services to graduate recruitment, admissions and students services and overall operations of the TGS office. The student assistant will assist with general office duties, data research, and assist with events hosted by TGS. Read more Plumber/Steamfitter Lead 20002251 Harrisonburg, Virginia Business Services Facilities / Skilled Trades Full-time Staff (Classified) James Madison University's Facilities Management Is currently hiring for a Plumber/Steamfitter Lead. This position will perform master level technical tasks in plumbing, gas , fire sprinkler and steam fitting trades. Read more Director and Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Clinical Mental Health Counseling M.A./Ed.S. Program 20002218 Harrisonburg, Virginia College of Health and Behavioral Studies Director / Unit Head Instructional / Teaching Faculty Other Instructional / Teaching Faculty The Counseling Programs at James Madison University are seeking an exceptional Counselor Educator to join the award‐winning faculty in the Department of Graduate Psychology and serve as the Program Director for our Clinical Mental Health Counseling M.A./Ed.S. Program. Our CACREP‐accredited programs include Clinical Mental Health Counseling M.A./Ed.S., School Counseling M.Ed./Ed.S., and Counseling and Supervision Ph.D. The full‐time (10 month), tenure track position will start in August 2027, and will be filled at the rank of advanced Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor. Read more Registered Nurse - 9-Month Position 20002257 Harrisonburg, Virginia Health and Wellbeing Health Center Full-time Staff (Classified) The University Health Center provides a comprehensive array of health care services and health education programs to JMU students. Included in our health care services are several medical clinics, a pharmacy, a medical laboratory, and other programs that provide services for more than 30,000 patient encounters a year. UHC practices evidence-based medicine in a confidential, welcoming environment.\n\nThis role offers an inspiring opportunity for nursing professionals to elevate care standards, strengthen a culture of compassion and excellence, alongside a talented clinical team dedicated to patient advocacy and evidence-based practice. At the UHC, you will have the chance to shape the future of campus healthcare, mentor the next generation of nursing professionals, and champion initiatives that meaningfully impact student health and well-being. Read more Arboretum Student Writer - IE 20002256 Harrisonburg, Virginia Business Services Student Employment Institutional Employment The Edith J. Carrier Arboretum at James Madison University curates and cares for a living laboratory of forest, naturalized areas, and gardens to promote: \n•\tHealthy landscapes and watersheds\n•\tResearch and education\n•\tOutdoor connection for all ages\n\nThe Arboretum is hiring a student writer position, designed as a work-based learning experience with opportunity to progress in responsibility and leadership over time. This student will work under the Arboretum Community Engagement Specialist. This position offers up to 15 hours per week. Read more Student House Managers - IE 20002252 Harrisonburg, Virginia College of Visual and Performing Arts Student Employment Institutional Employment James Madison University’s Forbes Center for the Performing Arts is seeking for two (2) new Student House Managers to provide front-of-house support for all events taking place in the Forbes Center that have patrons in attendance. Read more Student Writing Assistant - FWS 20002253 Harrisonburg, Virginia Constituent Engagement and Sustained Giving Student Employment Federal Work Study The Office of Alumni Relations is seeking an outstanding student to assist with story development, interviewing and content creation/editing. The student assistant should have excellent written storytelling skills, knowledge of AP style and be comfortable interviewing alumni.\n\nThe Student Writing Assistant must be available to work 10 hours per week (to be determined based on availability) between the hours of 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m., Monday through Friday within the Leeolou Alumni Center. Based on the availability of individuals being interviewed, the student assistant might have to conduct interviews outside the normal work hours. Read more Tenure-Track Assistant Professor, Developmental Biology 20002241 Harrisonburg, Virginia College of Science and Mathematics Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty The Department of Biology at James Madison University invites applications for a 10-month tenure-track Assistant Professor position with expertise in Developmental Biology. This is a full-time position with an anticipated start date of August 2027. \n\nThe successful candidate will join a thriving community of more than 60 biologists with broad sub-disciplinary diversity and will expand this diversity through expertise in evolutionary development (evo-devo). Research areas of interest include, but are not limited to, comparative and experimental embryology, developmental physiology, and eco-evo-devo (e.g., ecotoxicology). Details about existing faculty research expertise are available at: https://www.jmu.edu/biology/graduate/research-opportunities.shtml). Collaborative scholarship with other faculty members within and beyond the department is encouraged.\n \nThe department is committed to increasing the success of all students by creating and sustaining welcoming learning environments in and out of the classroom. The successful candidate will be expected to exemplify these principles in their teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and service to the institution. Please visit our website at http://www.jmu.edu/biology/ for more information about the department. Read more Promotores de Salud Program Coordinator (Part-Time) 20002248 Harrisonburg, Virginia College of Health and Behavioral Studies Other Part-time - Wage / Part-time Salaried The Promotores de Salud (PDS) Coordinator will play a key role in educating and empowering local communities about safe fish consumption practices. They will serve as a liaison between public health organizations, local communities, and individuals, particularly targeting populations that rely on fish as a dietary staple. The role involves providing culturally sensitive education on safe fish consumption, contaminant risks, and overall health, in alignment with environmental health and food safety guidelines. Read more Student Assistant - FWS 20002250 Harrisonburg, Virginia College of Education Student Employment Federal Work Study Closing on: Sep 8 2026 Student Assistant in the Education Support Center. Read more Recruitment and Employment Services Assistant (Part-Time) 20002243 Harrisonburg, Virginia Human Resources, Training and Performance Administrative / Office Staff Human resources Part-time - Wage / Part-time Salaried James Madison University’s Office of Human Resources is accepting applications for a part-time Recruitment and Employment Services Assistant. This position is responsible for providing a high level of customer service to both internal and external customers as well as administrative support to the Recruitment and Employment Services team.\n\nThis is an in-person position scheduled to work an average of 29 hours per week throughout the calendar year. Work hours are between 8:00 a.m. and 5:00 p.m., Monday through Friday. This position is not eligible for benefits. Read more Arboretum Landscape/Student Engagement Aide - IE 20002249 Harrisonburg, Virginia Business Services Student Employment Institutional Employment The Edith J. Carrier Arboretum at James Madison University is accepting applications for JMU students for the position of Student Engagement Aide. These positions will be under the supervision of the Student Engagement Lead for up to, but not exceeding, 15 hours per week between 7am-3pm Monday through Friday. Read more Talent Development Intern - IE 20002246 Harrisonburg, Virginia Human Resources, Training and Performance Student Employment Institutional Employment Closing on: Sep 7 2026 JMU Talent Development (TD) is seeking an undergraduate or graduate intern to assist the department with special projects and events related to the training and development of AP Faculty, classified staff, and wage employees at JMU.  \n\nThis is a part-time wage position working an average of 15 hours per week over the school year (32 weeks) with no benefits. Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background investigation. Students with strong organizational and business analysis skills are encouraged to apply. Read more Assistant Director, Academic Resources 20002245 Harrisonburg, Virginia Academic Affairs Unit Other Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) Closing on: Sep 30 2026 The Assistant Director of Academic Resources provides leadership, coordination, and oversight of administrative and operational functions supporting Academic Affairs. Working closely with the Director of Academic Resources, this position manages personnel administration, recruitment and hiring processes, salary analysis, budget coordination, payroll administration, data reporting, and strategic initiatives. The role serves as a primary liaison among Academic Affairs, Human Resources, Finance, Payroll, and university leadership to ensure efficient operations and informed decision making. The Assistant Director also leads Academic Affairs' participation in Oracle HCM/ERP initiatives, business process improvement efforts, and change management activities while supporting divisional priorities and university goals. Read more TRIO Educational Talent Search Advisor 20002247 Harrisonburg, Virginia Access and Enrollment Other Full-time Staff (Classified) TRIO Talent Search Advisors partner with campus and community colleagues to identify and assist first generation income eligible students in 6th through 12th grade who attend local middle schools and high schools and want to continue with their post-secondary education. The program provides academic, career and financial aid counseling to participants. The goal of Talent Search is to increase the rate at which participants complete secondary education and enroll in and graduate from institutions of postsecondary education.\n\nThe Advisor works directly works with the students, assisting them with academic class scheduling, implementing workshops, developing and implementing educational field trips and college tours, providing college application and financial aid assistance. Read more Student Financial, Data & Operational Support Assistant for Academic Affairs  - IE 20002244 Harrisonburg, Virginia Academic Affairs Unit Student Employment Institutional Employment Provide administrative, analytical and technical support to Academic Affairs leadership by assisting with budget management, financial reporting, data analysis, electronic workflows and records management. Work closely with AA staff to support fiscal transparency, reporting accuracy and process efficiency. Well-suited for students interested in business/data analysis, finance, accounting, information system, or public or higher education administration. Read more Communications and Advertising Specialist - School of Media Arts and Design 20002242 Harrisonburg, Virginia College of Arts and Letters Administrative / Office Staff Full-time Staff (Classified) The School of Media Arts and Design (SMAD) is accepting applications for a Communications and Marketing Specialist. This person will work with the Director and Associate Director to develop and coordinate advertising and outreach strategies aimed especially at students, prospective students and alumni. This staff member will also mentor and help coordinate SMAD student workers assigned to communications-related roles. Read more JMU Police Cadet - IE 20002238 Harrisonburg, Virginia Police and Public Safety Student Employment Institutional Employment Closing on: Dec 14 2026 JMU Police Cadets will patrol campus and work special events to ensure the safety and welfare of the JMU community and all visitors to JMU. All Cadets will be under the direct supervision of a cadet supervisor and program coordinator. Cadets will at times perform their duties with a high degree of independence, exercising considerable judgement, tact, and integrity in the completion of their responsibilities. Read more Academic Unit Head, Geology & Environmental Science 20002240 Harrisonburg, Virginia College of Science and Mathematics Director / Unit Head Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty James Madison University (JMU) invites applications for the position of Academic Unit Head (AUH) of the Department of Geology & Environmental Science, to begin July 1, 2027. This is a tenure track, 12-month, primarily administrative position at the rank of Professor or Associate Professor, with opportunities to teach, conduct research, and/or lead in their discipline. Application review will begin November 2, 2026, and the position is open until filled.\n\nThe Department of Geology and Environmental Science at James Madison University offers bachelor’s degrees in Geology and Environmental Earth Science for approximately 110 majors in our multi-track baccalaureate-only program, as well as minors in Geology, Climate Science, and Geophysics. In addition, we support interdisciplinary minors in Environmental Science and Data Analytics and prepare students for Earth Science teaching careers. We also offer a capstone summer field course. Faculty teach within the major and contribute significantly to General Education at JMU. Our students find placement in private sector and public service careers, and graduate studies through a strong network of professional and alumni connections.\n\nOur 15 full-time and three adjunct faculty members engage in teaching and research in the areas of Solid Earth Materials and Tectonics; Climate and Ocean Science; Paleobiology, Environmental and Engineering Geology; and Geoscience Education and Geoheritage. Our faculty are supported by two full-time staff members and we have additional support in grant administration, scientific computing, and media design. Read more General Maintenance Senior Technician - Second Shift 20002231 Harrisonburg, Virginia Business Services Facilities / Skilled Trades Full-time Staff (Classified) Facilities Management at JMU is currently accepting applications for a General Maintenance Senior Technician. This is a 2nd shift position. Read more Director of Major Gifts - Duke Club 20002230 Harrisonburg, Virginia Intercollegiate Athletics Athletics Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) James Madison University, a Division I member of the NCAA and Sun Belt Conference, the Duke Club is seeking a Director of Major Gifts to work within a highly competitive program. This is a full-time position with a comprehensive benefits package. Read more Marketing Assistant (Part-Time) - Forbes Center for the Performing Arts 20002237 Harrisonburg, Virginia College of Visual and Performing Arts Communications / Marketing Part-time - Wage / Part-time Salaried The Forbes Center for the Performing Arts at James Madison University is seeking a creative, organized, and detail-oriented part-time Marketing Assistant to support the planning, execution, and evaluation of marketing efforts for the Center’s performances and events. \n\nWorking closely with the Director of Marketing and Branding, this position will help increase awareness of Forbes Center programming, drive ticket sales, grow audience engagement, and strengthen the Center’s digital presence. \n\nThis position will provide hands-on experience in visual and performing arts marketing, digital marketing, social media, email marketing, audience development, advertising, content creation, and marketing analytics. Read more Family Education Specialist (Part-Time, Three Positions) - Shenandoah Valley Migrant Education Program 20002235 Harrisonburg, Virginia College of Health and Behavioral Studies Other Part-time - Wage / Part-time Salaried The Shenandoah Valley Migrant Education Program (SVMEP) is hiring for three part-time Family Education Specialist (FES) positions. These positions will each serve one of the following areas in the program’s region:\n\n• Northwestern Region: Rockingham County, Shenandoah County, Winchester City, Frederick County, Augusta County, Waynesboro City, Highland County\n• Southern Region: Grayson County, Galax City, Carroll County, Campbell County\n• Eastern Region: Henrico County, Fredericksburg Count, Richmond City, Alexandria City, Cumberland County, Culpeper County, Fairfax County, Nelson County, Albemarle County\n\nThese positions are eligible for telework. Regions may shift depending on where new migrant families enroll. \n\nSVMEP provides quality academic support services & advocacy to migrant families to aid the students in achieving their educational goals. SVMEP is one of many programs within the Institute for Innovation in Health & Human Services (IIHHS). IIHHS is a forward-thinking & dynamic organization that strives to cultivate a shared sense of purpose in building healthier and safer communities where all individuals can thrive and flourish. IIHHS is housed within JMU’s College of Health & Behavioral Studies (CHBS).\n\nCHBS is committed to shaping a forward-thinking & dynamic environment by refining policies, practices, and processes that strengthen our community, drive real-world advancement, and maintain spaces conducive to individual and collective growth. Through education, scholarship, and service, individuals are inspired to make responsible and meaningful contributions to the college, campus, local community, and broader world. Join us in fostering collaboration and innovation as we grow a dynamic college that embodies an atmosphere of belonging, champions excellence, and shares a sense of purpose. JMU is an equal opportunity employer committed to fostering a thriving environment where a wide range of perspectives are embraced, and fairness is upheld. Read more Arboretum Landscape & Horticulture Aide - IE 20002232 Harrisonburg, Virginia Business Services Student Employment Institutional Employment The Edith J. Carrier Arboretum at James Madison University is accepting applications for JMU students for the position of Arboretum Landscape & Horticulture Student aide. These positions will be under the supervision of the Arboretum Landscape Supervisor for up to, but not exceeding, 15 hours per week between 7am-3pm Monday through Friday. Read more Communications Content Assistant - Student FWS 20002236 Harrisonburg, Virginia Advancement Marketing Student Employment Federal Work Study Kickstart your storytelling career while you’re taking classes at JMU!\n\nJMU’s Philanthropic Communications team is looking for a curious, detail-oriented Communications Content Assistant to join our collaborative, fast-paced environment. In this role, you’ll research and/or be assigned to write stories that appear across campus and to our alumni and donors. While sharpening your journalistic voice and building a strong writing portfolio, you’ll be paid to interview students, faculty and alumni, cover events and build web content. If you love a good story, write cleanly under AP style and want hands-on experience with professional marketing and fundraising communications, this is your opportunity!\n\nHours:\n- This position is 10-12 hours per week.\n- Hours must be worked between 8 a.m. and 5 p.m. Monday through Friday, during the semester. (We will determine your work schedule based on your availability.)\n- Provided you continue to remain eligible for Federal Work Study, it may be possible for you to retain this position for future fall and/or spring semesters.\n\nWork Location: Sonner Hall (next to College of Business) Read more Administrative Assistant, AVP Research & Scholarship 20002226 Harrisonburg, Virginia Vice President - REDI Research Full-time Staff (Classified) JMU research contributes to our understanding of the world, drives innovation, develops solutions to global challenges, promotes collaborations, shapes our educational approaches and provides student learning opportunities in and beyond the classroom. The Division of Research, Economic Development & Innovation (REDI) is JMU’s central research division and supports faculty-scholars, students and staff engaged in a rich diversity of creative and intellectual endeavors across and between disciplines.  REDI is accepting applications for an Administrative Assistant to join our team.  The Administrative Assistant serves the Associate Vice President for Research & Scholarship by providing executive-level administrative support, coordinating office operations, coordinating communications and stakeholder engagement, supporting data gathering and reporting, and coordinating event and other project support.  The Administrative Assistant will also support collaboration and communication across university leadership, faculty, research centers, and external partners for strategic initiatives related to research development and institutional engagement. Read more Assistant Professor, School of Accounting 20002207 Harrisonburg, Virginia College of Business Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty James Madison University’s School of Accounting (SOA) invites applications for an experienced tenure-track Assistant Professor position starting Fall 2027. Advanced assistant professors are also encouraged to apply. We invite qualified applicants to teach and conduct research in any area of accounting with a preference for teaching financial/governmental or accounting information systems (AIS)/data analytics/technology. \n\nThe SOA offers the BBA and MSA degrees and first received separate AACSB accounting accreditation in 1985. The SOA’s faculty members work together in a highly collegial environment and have published in high-quality journals. The SOA has strong ties to the profession and is viewed as a prime recruiting school by employers. Read more EY Suite Front Desk Student Assistant - FWS 20002206 Harrisonburg, Virginia College of Business Student Employment Federal Work Study The EY Suite Front Desk Student Assistant serves as the primary point of contact for students, faculty, prospective students/families, and visitors to the Office of Professional Development and Undergraduate Programs Suite. This position plays a vital role in supporting the daily operations of the office while promoting a welcoming and professional environment for both the office and the College of Business\n\nFront Desk Student Assistant\nOffice of Professional Development and Undergraduate Programs (EY Suite)\nHours: Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–5:00 PM (Flexible shifts within this timeframe) Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 89 in total ‹ 1 2 3 › Privacy Policy Quick Links Accessibility at JMU Application Instructions Notice of Availability - Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Perm Notices Student Employment Employment Posters © 2026 JAMES MADISON UNIVERSITY Before You Go.. Would You Like To Sign Up For Job Alerts? First Name (required) 4e4db4f0 Last Name (required) 3d834681 Email (required) 692f34c9 Job Alert f42a2c44 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Employment Type Locations Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
