    "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/orientation-peer-adviser-opa-ie-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Orientation Peer Adviser (OPA)",
      "description": "Orientation Peer Adviser (OPA) - IE - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Home Explore JMU Benefits Navigate JMU Job Search My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode Orientation Peer Adviser (OPA) - IE 20002293 Health and Wellbeing Student Employment Institutional Employment Opening on: Sep 24 2026 Closing on: Oct 30 2026 Student Affairs 100165 - 1st Yr Experience/Orientation Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: Orientation Peer Adviser (OPA) - IE State Role Title: Institutional Employment/Federal Work Study Position Type: Institutional Employment Position Status: Part-Time FLSA Status: Exempt: Not Eligible for Overtime College/Division: Health and Wellbeing Department: 100165 - 1st Yr Experience/Orientation Pay Band: Pay Rate: Stipend Specify Range or Amount: $4555 (pre-tax) Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? No Beginning Review Date: About JMU: Situated in the heart of Virginia’s beautiful Shenandoah Valley, the city of Harrisonburg is a vibrant community with a population of approximately 52,000. Harrisonburg is conveniently located approximately 120 miles from Washington, D.C. and Richmond, VA. JMU is a selective, public institution with a growing national reputation for offering experiences that lead to an outstanding education and supportive environment for students, faculty and staff. The student body includes approximately 21,000 undergraduate and 1,800 graduate students, with over 1,000 full-time instructional faculty. JMU offers thriving programs in the liberal arts, science and technology, and professional disciplines at the undergraduate, master’s and doctoral levels. JMU has achieved national recognition for the high quality of its academic programs, focus on maintaining strong student/faculty interaction, and innovative faculty research. General Information: Want to make a difference at JMU? As an Orientation Peer Adviser, you'll welcome new students and their supporters during Summer Orientation and the Weeks of Welcome and serve as a trusted resource throughout their transition to college. By sharing your experiences and building meaningful connections, you'll help new Dukes feel supported, confident, and ready to succeed. If you're passionate about helping others and proud to be a Duke, apply to join the OPA team! Duties and Responsibilities: Attend and actively participate in all required O&T programming, including but not limited to: OPA spring workshops, spring overnight retreat, training, and events; FROG interviews and training; Summer Orientation sessions; and Weeks of Welcome training and programming. Assist incoming students in developing positive academic habits, peer relationships, and personal adjustment to JMU through small & large group discussions, individual peer interactions, and presentations. Assist parents, family members, and supporters of students in the transition to JMU through positive interactions. Serve as a peer mentor for First yeaR Orientation Guides (FROGs). This includes assisting in the FROG recruitment and selection process, communicating with FROGs, training, supervising, and evaluating FROGs during Weeks of Welcome. Demonstrate leadership by maintaining high energy and enthusiasm throughout long days, being flexible in a fast-paced environment, and showcasing a commitment to excellence. Qualifications: Must be enrolled full-time as an undergraduate student, not studying abroad during the 2027 spring, summer, or fall semester, and will not graduate until December 2027. Must be a JMU student in good academic AND disciplinary standing. A commitment to creating a welcoming and inclusive environment for all An effective and clear communicator with supervisors and peers Authenticity, flexibility, and dedication. Desire and ability to work effectively in a team-oriented environment Must be able to participate in the weekly, mandatory team training every Friday from 3:00-5:00pm (Jan 29-April 30) Must be able to participate in an overnight, off-campus spring retreat. Our office will cover all costs. (Dates have not been finalized, but tentatively Feb 5-7 or Feb 12-14.) Must be able to participate in all summer orientation dates. (Specific dates to be provided when available) Additional Posting Information: Compensation and benefits: Stipend: $4555 (pre-tax) Meals during Orientation programming and summer trainings Free housing in Apartments on Grace during Summer Orientation dates and training Orientation & Transition branded apparel ** By submitting this application, you authorize the Office of Orientation & Transition to review your university disciplinary records with the Office of Student Accountability and Restorative Practices for the purposes of confirming your disciplinary standing with James Madison University. You acknowledge and agree that this authorization will remain in effect during the term of your contract/involvement if chosen for this position. Conditions of Employment: E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are a student with a disability and need assistance please contact the Office of Disability Services at (540) 568-6705 or disability-svcs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the Office of Disability Services, located in the Student Success Center, Suite 1202 and they will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Recently Posted Jobs Associate Director, Research and Public Health 20002267 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) The Institute for Innovation in Health and Human Services (IIHHS) is accepting applications for a full-time Associate Director of Research and Public Health.\n\nThe Associate Director serves on the IIHHS Leadership Team, and takes a lead role in IIHHS strategic initiatives related to research and evaluation. This position also supervises and contributes to public health evaluation efforts done in partnership with the State, and is responsible for collaborating on grants to continue the public health research activities conducted out of IIHHS. This position also assists in grant applications to continue and grow our work across the Institute, and particularly in the areas of Research and Public Health. This role includes mentoring faculty and students as collaborators on research projects, and supports in-house evaluation efforts to build program capacity for evaluation. The Associate Director is a thought partner for and leads efforts to document social impact of IIHHS. The Associate Director supports the annual reporting efforts of IIHHS, including helping to strengthen and disseminate the annual report survey, preparing the data for the Director to include in the written annual report, and supporting data visualization efforts.\n\nIIHHS is seeking a creative, self-starting team member, who is effective working alone and as part of a team. The Associate Director supervises and works collaboratively with the PT Operations Coordinator, and also works collaboratively with colleagues across the Institute. The Associate Director ensures that all fiscal and personnel functions of the department operate at optimum efficiency, that grant funding supports program operations, and that deliverables stay on schedule and within budget. The Associate Director reports to the Director of IIHHS and provides fiscal and administrative support for areas and positions within the department.\n\nThis is not a remote/telework position. Student Case Administrator - Restorative Practices - IE 20002325 Student Employment Institutional Employment Student Case Administrators (SCAs) are undergraduate students who conduct one-on-one Individual Accountability Case Reviews for students who are alleged to have violated university policy. In Individual Accountability Case Reviews, SCAs evaluate evidence to determine whether or not the Responding Party is responsible for violating policy and, if applicable, assign outcomes. Student Case Administrators are undergraduate staff members in the Office of Student Accountability and Restorative Practices who participate in staff training and professional development; assist with various programs, outreach opportunities, and educational programs; and collaborate in the recruitment and selection of staff and volunteers. Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director 20002311 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty The Department of Health Professions in the College of Health and Behavioral Studies (CHBS) at James Madison University invites applications for Graduate Program Director of the Physician Assistant Studies program at the rank of Associate or Full Professor of Practice. This is a renewable term appointment. Accredited by ARC-PA, the program boasts a 98% first-time PANCE pass rate over the past five years and is supported by a stable, experienced faculty. The position offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across Health Professions programs and throughout the College. The preferred start date is January 1, 2027, with some flexibility based on candidate availability and institutional needs.\n\nThe successful candidate will join an engaged faculty at one of the nation's leading public universities. CHBS is committed to fostering a welcoming, innovative environment that supports individual and collective growth through education, scholarship, and service. Learn more about CHBS at https://www.jmu.edu/chbs/about.shtml Privacy Policy Quick Links Accessibility at JMU Application Instructions Notice of Availability - Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Perm Notices Student Employment Employment Posters © 2026 JAMES MADISON UNIVERSITY Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/rta-lecturer-health-sciences-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states-f4f07941-2b5e-4580-9be8-483010b628c0": {
      "title": "RTA Lecturer, Health Sciences",
      "description": "RTA Lecturer, Health Sciences - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Home Explore JMU Benefits Navigate JMU Job Search My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode RTA Lecturer, Health Sciences 20002313 College of Health and Behavioral Studies Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Opening on: Sep 23 2026 Academic Affairs 100056 - Health Sciences Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: RTA Lecturer, Health Sciences State Role Title: N/A Position Type: Instructional / Teaching Faculty Position Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Exempt: Not Eligible for Overtime College/Division: College of Health and Behavioral Studies Department: 100056 - Health Sciences Pay Band: N/A Pay Rate: Commensurate with Experience Specify Range or Amount: Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? No Beginning Review Date: 10/24/2026 About JMU: Mission We are a community committed to preparing students to be educated and enlightened citizens who lead productive and meaningful lives. Vision To be the national model for the engaged university: engaged with ideas and the world. Who We Are Situated in the heart of Virginia’s beautiful Shenandoah Valley, the city of Harrisonburg is a vibrant community with a population of approximately 52,000. Harrisonburg is conveniently located approximately 120 miles from Washington, D.C. and Richmond, VA. JMU is a selective, public institution with a growing national reputation for offering experiences that lead to an outstanding education and supportive environment for students, faculty and staff. The student body includes approximately 21,000 undergraduate and 1,800 graduate students, with over 1,000 full-time instructional faculty. JMU offers thriving programs in the liberal arts, science and technology, and professional disciplines at the undergraduate, master’s and doctoral levels. JMU has achieved national recognition for the high quality of its academic programs, focus on maintaining strong student/faculty interaction, and innovative faculty research. General Information: The Department of Health Sciences in the College of Health and Behavioral Studies at James Madison University offers a dynamic Bachelor of Science in Health Sciences curriculum. The Health Sciences major is designed for students interested in understanding the causes of disease, strategies for promoting wellness and behavior change, and the scientific basis and methodologies for analyzing health concerns for both individuals and populations. Upon degree completion, graduates are prepared for immediate employment in multiple allied health areas or a pathway to graduate studies in a variety of disciplines, including medicine, optometry, pharmacy, nursing, public health, and other professional preparation programs. The successful candidate will join a strong and engaged faculty at one of the nation’s outstanding public universities. Because we educate future healthcare professionals, we recognize our ethical responsibility to educate students and to advocate for dignity, caring and fair treatment for all. Health Sciences faculty are committed to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Our college actively engages in practices that promote a welcoming learning environment and foster a sense of belonging and student success, where colleagues can thrive in teaching, research, and service. We invite applications for a Renewable Term Appointment at the Lecturer rank to join our team. The position has an anticipated start date in January 2027 (for spring semester classes). RANK Lecturer, Renewable Term Appointment, 10-Month Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will: • Teach multiple in-person undergraduate Health Sciences courses within the general education curriculum, including large-enrollment sections (160 students each) of HTH 100 Personal Wellness, a 3-credit course option in the General Education – Well Being Area • Teach undergraduate courses within the Health Sciences major curriculum, such as Introduction to Health Sciences and Population Health Determinants • Develop and deliver engaging and evidence-based instruction appropriate for undergraduate students • Use appropriate instructional technologies and learning management systems • Provide student support through office hours and other appropriate instructional activities • Engage in ongoing professional development related to teaching and the Health Sciences discipline (e.g. attending professional conferences, maintaining CEUs, and/or maintaining certification credentials) • Participate in service at the departmental, college, and university levels Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications • Earned master's degree in health sciences, health education and promotion, public health, or related field prior to the start date • Evidence of effective undergraduate teaching or relevant instructional experience Preferred Qualifications • Prior university-level teaching experience • Experience teaching large-enrollment undergraduate courses • Experience teaching Personal Wellness, health promotion, public health, health education, or related coursework • Evidence of student-centered teaching practices • Experience with curriculum or course development • Prior professional service at the department, college, university, or professional association level • Evidence of professional development Additional Posting Information: Applicants will need to submit the following: (1) completed faculty profile; (2) cover letter describing your experiences and accomplishments related to teaching; (3) teaching philosophy including a statement highlighting your use of engaging practices related to teaching, scholarship, service, advising, and/or mentoring students; (4) curriculum vitae; and (5) names and contact information of three professional references. Inquiries may be made to Theresa Enyeart Smith, Search Committee Chair, Department of Health Sciences, 235 Martin Luther King Jr. Way, MSC 4301, James Madison University, Harrisonburg, VA 22807, email enyeartm@jmu.edu or phone 540-568-3951. Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 22c6b136 Last Name (required) 21d732db Email (required) 00af263c Job Alert 7786f4d8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Know someone who would be interested in this job? First Name (required) 729a42f3 Last Name (required) e53305dd Email (required) 8ea4b8ca Who would you like to send this job to? 41c1e95d Refer Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recently Posted Jobs Associate Director, Research and Public Health 20002267 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) The Institute for Innovation in Health and Human Services (IIHHS) is accepting applications for a full-time Associate Director of Research and Public Health.\n\nThe Associate Director serves on the IIHHS Leadership Team, and takes a lead role in IIHHS strategic initiatives related to research and evaluation. This position also supervises and contributes to public health evaluation efforts done in partnership with the State, and is responsible for collaborating on grants to continue the public health research activities conducted out of IIHHS. This position also assists in grant applications to continue and grow our work across the Institute, and particularly in the areas of Research and Public Health. This role includes mentoring faculty and students as collaborators on research projects, and supports in-house evaluation efforts to build program capacity for evaluation. The Associate Director is a thought partner for and leads efforts to document social impact of IIHHS. The Associate Director supports the annual reporting efforts of IIHHS, including helping to strengthen and disseminate the annual report survey, preparing the data for the Director to include in the written annual report, and supporting data visualization efforts.\n\nIIHHS is seeking a creative, self-starting team member, who is effective working alone and as part of a team. The Associate Director supervises and works collaboratively with the PT Operations Coordinator, and also works collaboratively with colleagues across the Institute. The Associate Director ensures that all fiscal and personnel functions of the department operate at optimum efficiency, that grant funding supports program operations, and that deliverables stay on schedule and within budget. The Associate Director reports to the Director of IIHHS and provides fiscal and administrative support for areas and positions within the department.\n\nThis is not a remote/telework position. Student Case Administrator - Restorative Practices - IE 20002325 Student Employment Institutional Employment Student Case Administrators (SCAs) are undergraduate students who conduct one-on-one Individual Accountability Case Reviews for students who are alleged to have violated university policy. In Individual Accountability Case Reviews, SCAs evaluate evidence to determine whether or not the Responding Party is responsible for violating policy and, if applicable, assign outcomes. Student Case Administrators are undergraduate staff members in the Office of Student Accountability and Restorative Practices who participate in staff training and professional development; assist with various programs, outreach opportunities, and educational programs; and collaborate in the recruitment and selection of staff and volunteers. Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director 20002311 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty The Department of Health Professions in the College of Health and Behavioral Studies (CHBS) at James Madison University invites applications for Graduate Program Director of the Physician Assistant Studies program at the rank of Associate or Full Professor of Practice. This is a renewable term appointment. Accredited by ARC-PA, the program boasts a 98% first-time PANCE pass rate over the past five years and is supported by a stable, experienced faculty. The position offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across Health Professions programs and throughout the College. The preferred start date is January 1, 2027, with some flexibility based on candidate availability and institutional needs.\n\nThe successful candidate will join an engaged faculty at one of the nation's leading public universities. CHBS is committed to fostering a welcoming, innovative environment that supports individual and collective growth through education, scholarship, and service. Learn more about CHBS at https://www.jmu.edu/chbs/about.shtml Apply Now First Name (required) f6f1e490 Last Name (required) 46e50903 Email (required) e40cb3ac Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Privacy Policy Quick Links Accessibility at JMU Application Instructions Notice of Availability - Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Perm Notices Student Employment Employment Posters © 2026 JAMES MADISON UNIVERSITY Before You Go.. Would You Like To Sign Up For Job Alerts? First Name (required) f50bb8f5 Last Name (required) f9d67c76 Email (required) df9c0b32 Job Alert 39e5298e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve 