    "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/maintenance-and-planner-scheduler-two-positions-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Maintenance and Planner/Scheduler (Two Positions)",
      "description": "Maintenance and Planner/Scheduler (Two Positions) - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Home Explore JMU Benefits Navigate JMU Job Search My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode Maintenance and Planner/Scheduler (Two Positions) 20002316 Business Services Facilities / Skilled Trades Full-time Staff (Classified) Opening on: Sep 23 2026 Administration and Finance 100250 - FM Administration Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: Maintenance and Planner/Scheduler (Two Positions) State Role Title: Policy and Planning Specialist I Position Type: Full-time Staff (Classified) Position Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Exempt: Not Eligible for Overtime College/Division: Business Services Department: 100250 - FM Administration Pay Band: 4 Pay Rate: Pay Range Specify Range or Amount: $55,000-$61,000 Is this a JMU only position? N/A Is this a grant-funded position? N/A Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? N/A Beginning Review Date: 10/1/2026 About JMU: At James Madison University (JMU), we’re more than just a publicly funded institution — we’re a vibrant, welcoming community located on a stunning campus where innovation, collaboration, and personal growth thrive. Our mission is to prepare students for a bright future, and we believe that starts with supporting the people who make it all possible: our employees. Why Work at JMU? We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your professional journey and personal wellbeing: • Generous Leave: Enjoy paid vacation, sick leave, parental leave, community service leave, and 19 paid holidays annually. • Comprehensive Health Coverage: Access high-quality health insurance options that fit your needs. • Retirement Options: Plan for your future with retirement benefits through the Virginia Retirement System. • Employee Well-Being: Our Balanced Dukes program promotes wellness and work-life integration through resources, events, and support. • Tuition Waiver Program: Advance your education with our tuition waiver program for undergraduate and graduate courses taken at JMU. At JMU, we believe in Being the Change — and that starts with creating an environment where you can grow, contribute meaningfully, and feel supported every step of the way. Discover what makes JMU a great place to work: bit.ly/JMUEmployment General Information: James Madison University Facilities Management is seeking applicants for our Maintenance and Planner/Scheduler positions. A successful candidate will independently schedule resources in support of maintenance, events, and projects by effectively communicating needs with customers, managers and supervisors. Duties and Responsibilities: Daily/Weekly Craft and Crew Scheduling: - Develops scheduled and repetitive work orders based on resource availability. - Provides zoned overviews of facility inspections through the coordination and direction of the senior planner. -Facilitate a weekly scheduling meeting involving all trade supervisors for reviewing the following weeks work and updating current work loads. - Set-up and track all internal maintenance projects to include time frames, budget, manpower availability, workload, and status. - Work with all campus departments along with the maintenance trades in developing a comprehensive summer schedule that includes all housekeeping, engineering, and shop projects and sweeps needed to be completed prior to students arriving. - Keep the Master Schedule up-to-date with all projects and events throughout the year. - Schedule in Resource 25 as needed for for maintenance procedures on campus. - Prepare and submit permits for required activities to the state for approval. - Post outages and closures on the FM web site when scheduled. - E-mail customers to confirm scheduled FM events that will involve their areas. - Ensures a timely review of the maintenance backlog. - Priority repairs are established based on work order priority status codes developed through the planner and customer feedback. Project Management Coordinator: - Works one-on-one with customers, contractors, managers and supervisors to develop scope of work and time frames. -Assures that the customer is aware of the permits that are required and that they are in place prior to project startup. -Forecast/Project current and future needs related to services, personnel, and equipment. Make recommendations to the Senior Planner. - Develops all paperwork to ensure data is accurately captured and a clear definition and scope of work is communicated with the customer and project team. - Ensures projects are developed and resource availability is scheduled. - Reviews all project and equipment type requests. - Develops an approval routing to ensure estimates are clearly communicated to customers and project team. -Coordinate FM crews and contractors working on in-house projects. - Have established policy and procedures related to costs associated with a project request and have established accounting procedures. Special Event Coordination: -Assist with event related activities for proper support by working with managers, supervisors, contractors, vendors and others as needed to ensure proper progression of the event. -Barrier management to ensure customer issues are addressed time Facilities & Campus Inspections: -Works with the inspection team, customers and Facilities Management in the inspection of a facilities with a comprehensive database -Develops annual inspection schedules to cyclical time frames have been developed with a comprehensive database established for management of cost analysis and future capital project development. -Employee may be required to temporarily work another shift based on business need. Qualifications: -Event, planning and scheduling knowledge related to a facilities environment and program management. -Estimating knowledge in residential and small commercial applications, to include electrical, plumbing, HVAC, paint, carpentry, etc. related to minor construction work. -Working knowledge and general training in a facilities and project management environment. -The ability to communicate with technical and program managers. -Skilled in resource planning, scheduling and estimating. Additional Posting Information: Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check and an acceptable MVR. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Recently Posted Jobs Associate Director, Research and Public Health 20002267 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) The Institute for Innovation in Health and Human Services (IIHHS) is accepting applications for a full-time Associate Director of Research and Public Health.\n\nThe Associate Director serves on the IIHHS Leadership Team, and takes a lead role in IIHHS strategic initiatives related to research and evaluation. This position also supervises and contributes to public health evaluation efforts done in partnership with the State, and is responsible for collaborating on grants to continue the public health research activities conducted out of IIHHS. This position also assists in grant applications to continue and grow our work across the Institute, and particularly in the areas of Research and Public Health. This role includes mentoring faculty and students as collaborators on research projects, and supports in-house evaluation efforts to build program capacity for evaluation. The Associate Director is a thought partner for and leads efforts to document social impact of IIHHS. The Associate Director supports the annual reporting efforts of IIHHS, including helping to strengthen and disseminate the annual report survey, preparing the data for the Director to include in the written annual report, and supporting data visualization efforts.\n\nIIHHS is seeking a creative, self-starting team member, who is effective working alone and as part of a team. The Associate Director supervises and works collaboratively with the PT Operations Coordinator, and also works collaboratively with colleagues across the Institute. The Associate Director ensures that all fiscal and personnel functions of the department operate at optimum efficiency, that grant funding supports program operations, and that deliverables stay on schedule and within budget. The Associate Director reports to the Director of IIHHS and provides fiscal and administrative support for areas and positions within the department.\n\nThis is not a remote/telework position. Student Case Administrator - Restorative Practices - IE 20002325 Student Employment Institutional Employment Student Case Administrators (SCAs) are undergraduate students who conduct one-on-one Individual Accountability Case Reviews for students who are alleged to have violated university policy. In Individual Accountability Case Reviews, SCAs evaluate evidence to determine whether or not the Responding Party is responsible for violating policy and, if applicable, assign outcomes. Student Case Administrators are undergraduate staff members in the Office of Student Accountability and Restorative Practices who participate in staff training and professional development; assist with various programs, outreach opportunities, and educational programs; and collaborate in the recruitment and selection of staff and volunteers. Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director 20002311 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty The Department of Health Professions in the College of Health and Behavioral Studies (CHBS) at James Madison University invites applications for Graduate Program Director of the Physician Assistant Studies program at the rank of Associate or Full Professor of Practice. This is a renewable term appointment. Accredited by ARC-PA, the program boasts a 98% first-time PANCE pass rate over the past five years and is supported by a stable, experienced faculty. The position offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across Health Professions programs and throughout the College. The preferred start date is January 1, 2027, with some flexibility based on candidate availability and institutional needs.\n\nThe successful candidate will join an engaged faculty at one of the nation's leading public universities. CHBS is committed to fostering a welcoming, innovative environment that supports individual and collective growth through education, scholarship, and service. Learn more about CHBS at https://www.jmu.edu/chbs/about.shtml Privacy Policy Quick Links Accessibility at JMU Application Instructions Notice of Availability - Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Perm Notices Student Employment Employment Posters © 2026 JAMES MADISON UNIVERSITY Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
