    "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-strategic-communication-public-relations-school-of-communication-studies-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Strategic Communication/Public Relations",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Strategic Communication/Public Relations - School of Communication Studies - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Home Explore JMU Benefits Navigate JMU Job Search My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode Assistant Professor, Strategic Communication/Public Relations - School of Communication Studies 20002318 College of Arts and Letters Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Opening on: Sep 23 2026 Academic Affairs 100017 - School of Communication Studies Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: Assistant Professor, Strategic Communication/Public Relations - School of Communication Studies State Role Title: N/A Position Type: Instructional / Teaching Faculty Position Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Exempt: Not Eligible for Overtime College/Division: College of Arts and Letters Department: 100017 - School of Communication Studies Pay Band: N/A Pay Rate: Commensurate with Experience Specify Range or Amount: Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? No Beginning Review Date: 10/26/2026 About JMU: Mission We are a community committed to preparing students to be educated and enlightened citizens who lead productive and meaningful lives. Vision To be the national model for the engaged university: engaged with ideas and the world. Who We Are Situated in the heart of Virginia’s beautiful Shenandoah Valley, the city of Harrisonburg is a vibrant community with a population of approximately 52,000. Harrisonburg is conveniently located approximately 120 miles from Washington, D.C. and Richmond, VA. JMU is a selective, public institution with a growing national reputation for offering experiences that lead to an outstanding education and supportive environment for students, faculty and staff. The student body includes approximately 21,000 undergraduate and 1,800 graduate students, with over 1,000 full-time instructional faculty. JMU offers thriving programs in the liberal arts, science and technology, and professional disciplines at the undergraduate, master’s and doctoral levels. JMU has achieved national recognition for the high quality of its academic programs, focus on maintaining strong student/faculty interaction, and innovative faculty research. General Information: The School of Communication Studies at James Madison University invites applications for a tenure-track Strategic Communication / Public Relations faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor. Employment begins in August 2027. We seek an innovative scholar and educator whose teaching, research, and professional experiences advance the study and practice of strategic communication and public relations. We welcome candidates who combine strong scholarly potential, excellent teaching, and professional or applied expertise and who can contribute to the School’s undergraduate public relations curriculum and graduate strategic communication program. The successful candidate will join a vibrant program with an active and award-winning PRSSA chapter and student-run public relations firm. The School’s Public Relations program has also been recognized by the PRWeek Awards, including an honorable mention for Education Program of the Year. These opportunities provide an exceptional environment for faculty to connect scholarship, teaching, mentoring, and professional practice. Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will: - teach a variety of public relations courses at the undergraduate level, including but not limited to, public relations writing, theory, research methods, and/or capstone courses. - teach strategic communication courses at the graduate level. - incorporate experiential, project-based, client-based, and/or community-engaged learning where appropriate. - maintain an active research program that contributes to the scholarly study of public relations and strategic communication. - publish scholarly work in appropriate peer-reviewed outlets and present research at professional and scholarly conferences. - pursue interdisciplinary research and external funding opportunities as appropriate to the candidate’s research agenda. - mentor and advise undergraduate and graduate students. - contribute to the School’s student professional development activities, including opportunities associated with PRSSA and Bluestone Communications, our student-run public relations firm. - participate in appropriate School, College, University, professional, and community service. We welcome candidates whose research advances the study of public relations and strategic communication through diverse theoretical, methodological, and interdisciplinary approaches. Expertise in digital and social media, emerging communication technologies, artificial intelligence, analytics, or other evolving areas of public relations practice and research is especially welcome. Preference will be given to candidates whose research and teaching expertise complements and expands the School’s strengths in organizational communication, sports communication, health communication, nonprofit communication, public affairs, and related areas. Qualifications: A PhD in Communication or a related field is required; ABD applicants with the degree near completion will be considered with the requirement that the degree be conferred by August 2027. Candidates must demonstrate evidence of teaching excellence and possess a record of continued or promising scholarly productivity. Preferred qualifications include: - professional experience in public relations, strategic communication, corporate communication, nonprofit communication, public affairs, agency practice, or a related field. - experience teaching public relations writing, research methods, campaigns, theory, capstone, digital/social media, analytics, or related courses. - expertise in digital and social media, emerging communication technologies, artificial intelligence, analytics, or other evolving areas of public relations practice and research. - experience pursuing external research funding or demonstrated potential to develop externally funded research. - experience with experiential, client-based, community-engaged, or applied teaching and scholarship. Additional Posting Information: Candidates should complete the online application and upload the following: -A letter of application that describes your research agenda and its trajectory, the public relations and strategic communication courses you are prepared to teach, and how your scholarship, teaching, and/or professional experience would contribute to the School's undergraduate and graduate programs -Evidence of teaching effectiveness (uploaded under \"Other Document #1\") -A copy of unofficial transcripts -Curriculum vitae -Names, phone numbers, and email addresses for three academic references Questions should be addressed to Dr. Chang Wan “Isaac” Woo (woocw@jmu.edu), the search chair. JMU’s Dual Career and Community Resources Program is available for candidates that will be relocating to the area. For more information, please visit https://bit.ly/2OTF1NG. Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) f84653ea Last Name (required) 67284d34 Email (required) 4af8d21c Job Alert e09150b4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Know someone who would be interested in this job? First Name (required) cc497f8d Last Name (required) a0229796 Email (required) 76855545 Who would you like to send this job to? 8dea3005 Refer Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recently Posted Jobs Associate Director, Research and Public Health 20002267 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) The Institute for Innovation in Health and Human Services (IIHHS) is accepting applications for a full-time Associate Director of Research and Public Health.\n\nThe Associate Director serves on the IIHHS Leadership Team, and takes a lead role in IIHHS strategic initiatives related to research and evaluation. This position also supervises and contributes to public health evaluation efforts done in partnership with the State, and is responsible for collaborating on grants to continue the public health research activities conducted out of IIHHS. This position also assists in grant applications to continue and grow our work across the Institute, and particularly in the areas of Research and Public Health. This role includes mentoring faculty and students as collaborators on research projects, and supports in-house evaluation efforts to build program capacity for evaluation. The Associate Director is a thought partner for and leads efforts to document social impact of IIHHS. The Associate Director supports the annual reporting efforts of IIHHS, including helping to strengthen and disseminate the annual report survey, preparing the data for the Director to include in the written annual report, and supporting data visualization efforts.\n\nIIHHS is seeking a creative, self-starting team member, who is effective working alone and as part of a team. The Associate Director supervises and works collaboratively with the PT Operations Coordinator, and also works collaboratively with colleagues across the Institute. The Associate Director ensures that all fiscal and personnel functions of the department operate at optimum efficiency, that grant funding supports program operations, and that deliverables stay on schedule and within budget. The Associate Director reports to the Director of IIHHS and provides fiscal and administrative support for areas and positions within the department.\n\nThis is not a remote/telework position. Student Case Administrator - Restorative Practices - IE 20002325 Student Employment Institutional Employment Student Case Administrators (SCAs) are undergraduate students who conduct one-on-one Individual Accountability Case Reviews for students who are alleged to have violated university policy. In Individual Accountability Case Reviews, SCAs evaluate evidence to determine whether or not the Responding Party is responsible for violating policy and, if applicable, assign outcomes. Student Case Administrators are undergraduate staff members in the Office of Student Accountability and Restorative Practices who participate in staff training and professional development; assist with various programs, outreach opportunities, and educational programs; and collaborate in the recruitment and selection of staff and volunteers. Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director 20002311 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty The Department of Health Professions in the College of Health and Behavioral Studies (CHBS) at James Madison University invites applications for Graduate Program Director of the Physician Assistant Studies program at the rank of Associate or Full Professor of Practice. This is a renewable term appointment. Accredited by ARC-PA, the program boasts a 98% first-time PANCE pass rate over the past five years and is supported by a stable, experienced faculty. The position offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across Health Professions programs and throughout the College. The preferred start date is January 1, 2027, with some flexibility based on candidate availability and institutional needs.\n\nThe successful candidate will join an engaged faculty at one of the nation's leading public universities. CHBS is committed to fostering a welcoming, innovative environment that supports individual and collective growth through education, scholarship, and service. Learn more about CHBS at https://www.jmu.edu/chbs/about.shtml Apply Now First Name (required) 1ea028d4 Last Name (required) 2bf82ba1 Email (required) 5fd86cdb Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Privacy Policy Quick Links Accessibility at JMU Application Instructions Notice of Availability - Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Perm Notices Student Employment Employment Posters © 2026 JAMES MADISON UNIVERSITY Before You Go.. Would You Like To Sign Up For Job Alerts? First Name (required) d0f93198 Last Name (required) ef8f3512 Email (required) e3365edf Job Alert f63db688 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-political-science-political-theory-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Political Science (Political Theory)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor- Political Science (Political Theory) - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Home Explore JMU Benefits Navigate JMU Job Search My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode Assistant Professor- Political Science (Political Theory) 20002319 College of Arts and Letters Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Opening on: Sep 23 2026 Academic Affairs 100033 - Political Science Department Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: Assistant Professor- Political Science (Political Theory) State Role Title: N/A Position Type: Instructional / Teaching Faculty Position Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Exempt: Not Eligible for Overtime College/Division: College of Arts and Letters Department: 100033 - Political Science Department Pay Band: N/A Pay Rate: Commensurate with Experience Specify Range or Amount: Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? No Beginning Review Date: 10/26/2026 About JMU: Mission We are a community committed to preparing students to be educated and enlightened citizens who lead productive and meaningful lives. Vision To be the national model for the engaged university: engaged with ideas and the world. Who We Are Situated in the heart of Virginia’s beautiful Shenandoah Valley, the city of Harrisonburg is a vibrant community with a population of approximately 52,000. Harrisonburg is conveniently located approximately 120 miles from Washington, D.C. and Richmond, VA. JMU is a selective, public institution with a growing national reputation for offering experiences that lead to an outstanding education and supportive environment for students, faculty and staff. The student body includes approximately 21,000 undergraduate and 1,800 graduate students, with over 1,000 full-time instructional faculty. JMU offers thriving programs in the liberal arts, science and technology, and professional disciplines at the undergraduate, master’s and doctoral levels. JMU has achieved national recognition for the high quality of its academic programs, focus on maintaining strong student/faculty interaction, and innovative faculty research. General Information: The Department of Political Science at James Madison University invites applications for one tenure track assistant professor position in Political Science with a specialization in Political Theory. Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will teach an introductory undergraduate course on Western Political Theory and upper-level undergraduate courses in Political Theory. The interest and ability to teach an upper-level class that investigates the intersection of political theory and law is desirable though not necessary, and we remain open to other course offerings in political theory. The standard teaching load is 3-2. The department includes undergraduate majors in Political Science, International Affairs, and Public Administration and graduate programs in Political Science and Public Administration. Faculty in the department also support a wide range of collaborative and interdisciplinary minors, including but not limited to those in: African, African American, and Diaspora Studies; Asian Studies; Environmental Science; Environmental Studies; Humanitarian Affairs; Latin American, Latinx, and Caribbean Studies; Legal Studies; Medieval and Renaissance Studies; Middle Eastern Communities and Migrations; Modern European Studies; Political Communication; and Women, Gender, and Sexuality Studies. Qualifications: Candidates should hold a Ph.D. or have ABD status with the degree near completion and should demonstrate excellence in teaching and research, as well as a commitment to fostering a welcoming and supportive scholarly environment. The position will begin in August 2027. Additional Posting Information: The College of Arts and Letters in which the Department of Political Science is located, enrolls over 3,100 undergraduate majors and about 150 graduate students across ten academic units in the humanities, social sciences, and communication studies. Home to several interdisciplinary centers and institutes, the College employs 270 full-time faculty. We embrace the teacher-scholar model, and encourage excellent applicants within our particular disciplines, as well as scholars and teachers eager to work across them. We look to enhance our existing interdisciplinary strengths and to extend our offerings in global cultures, politics, and religions, as well as in global justice, disability studies, legal studies, and digital humanities. Complete applications will include a cover letter, current CV, names and contact information for three professional references, a statement on teaching philosophy, and a statement on research interests (uploaded under \"other document #1\"). JMU’s Dual Career and Community Resources Program is available for candidates that will be relocating to the area. For more information, please visit https://bit.ly/2OTF1NG. Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 33760acc Last Name (required) 4f6ad28a Email (required) 9ff3050b Job Alert a078b71d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Know someone who would be interested in this job? First Name (required) a42fc5e3 Last Name (required) 96fc8a38 Email (required) d7554725 Who would you like to send this job to? 6e6d3965 Refer Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recently Posted Jobs Associate Director, Research and Public Health 20002267 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) The Institute for Innovation in Health and Human Services (IIHHS) is accepting applications for a full-time Associate Director of Research and Public Health.\n\nThe Associate Director serves on the IIHHS Leadership Team, and takes a lead role in IIHHS strategic initiatives related to research and evaluation. This position also supervises and contributes to public health evaluation efforts done in partnership with the State, and is responsible for collaborating on grants to continue the public health research activities conducted out of IIHHS. This position also assists in grant applications to continue and grow our work across the Institute, and particularly in the areas of Research and Public Health. This role includes mentoring faculty and students as collaborators on research projects, and supports in-house evaluation efforts to build program capacity for evaluation. The Associate Director is a thought partner for and leads efforts to document social impact of IIHHS. The Associate Director supports the annual reporting efforts of IIHHS, including helping to strengthen and disseminate the annual report survey, preparing the data for the Director to include in the written annual report, and supporting data visualization efforts.\n\nIIHHS is seeking a creative, self-starting team member, who is effective working alone and as part of a team. The Associate Director supervises and works collaboratively with the PT Operations Coordinator, and also works collaboratively with colleagues across the Institute. The Associate Director ensures that all fiscal and personnel functions of the department operate at optimum efficiency, that grant funding supports program operations, and that deliverables stay on schedule and within budget. The Associate Director reports to the Director of IIHHS and provides fiscal and administrative support for areas and positions within the department.\n\nThis is not a remote/telework position. Student Case Administrator - Restorative Practices - IE 20002325 Student Employment Institutional Employment Student Case Administrators (SCAs) are undergraduate students who conduct one-on-one Individual Accountability Case Reviews for students who are alleged to have violated university policy. In Individual Accountability Case Reviews, SCAs evaluate evidence to determine whether or not the Responding Party is responsible for violating policy and, if applicable, assign outcomes. Student Case Administrators are undergraduate staff members in the Office of Student Accountability and Restorative Practices who participate in staff training and professional development; assist with various programs, outreach opportunities, and educational programs; and collaborate in the recruitment and selection of staff and volunteers. Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director 20002311 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty The Department of Health Professions in the College of Health and Behavioral Studies (CHBS) at James Madison University invites applications for Graduate Program Director of the Physician Assistant Studies program at the rank of Associate or Full Professor of Practice. This is a renewable term appointment. Accredited by ARC-PA, the program boasts a 98% first-time PANCE pass rate over the past five years and is supported by a stable, experienced faculty. The position offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across Health Professions programs and throughout the College. The preferred start date is January 1, 2027, with some flexibility based on candidate availability and institutional needs.\n\nThe successful candidate will join an engaged faculty at one of the nation's leading public universities. CHBS is committed to fostering a welcoming, innovative environment that supports individual and collective growth through education, scholarship, and service. Learn more about CHBS at https://www.jmu.edu/chbs/about.shtml Apply Now First Name (required) 1c7b302e Last Name (required) 09aabb5b Email (required) 068b4499 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Privacy Policy Quick Links Accessibility at JMU Application Instructions Notice of Availability - Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Perm Notices Student Employment Employment Posters © 2026 JAMES MADISON UNIVERSITY Before You Go.. Would You Like To Sign Up For Job Alerts? First Name (required) b70001e4 Last Name (required) 7f8bf7b2 Email (required) 141c4654 Job Alert 1030dfa0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Employment Type Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
