    "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/peer-counselor-fws-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Peer Counselor",
      "description": "Peer Counselor - FWS - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Home Explore JMU Benefits Navigate JMU Job Search My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode Peer Counselor - FWS 20002315 Financial Aid and Scholarships Student Employment Federal Work Study Opening on: Sep 22 2026 Closing on: Oct 12 2026 Access and Enrollment 100179 - Financial Aid and Scholarships Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: Peer Counselor - FWS State Role Title: Institutional Employment/Federal Work Study Position Type: Federal Work Study Position Status: Part-Time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt: Eligible for Overtime College/Division: Financial Aid and Scholarships Department: 100179 - Financial Aid and Scholarships Pay Band: N/A Pay Rate: Hourly Specify Range or Amount: $13.77 Is this a JMU only position? N/A Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? N/A Beginning Review Date: 10/12/2026 About JMU: Situated in the heart of Virginia’s beautiful Shenandoah Valley, the city of Harrisonburg is a vibrant community with a population of approximately 52,000. Harrisonburg is conveniently located approximately 120 miles from Washington, D.C. and Richmond, VA. JMU is a selective, public institution with a growing national reputation for offering experiences that lead to an outstanding education and supportive environment for students, faculty and staff. The student body includes approximately 21,000 undergraduate and 1,800 graduate students, with over 1,000 full-time instructional faculty. JMU offers thriving programs in the liberal arts, science and technology, and professional disciplines at the undergraduate, master’s and doctoral levels. JMU has achieved national recognition for the high quality of its academic programs, focus on maintaining strong student/faculty interaction, and innovative faculty research. General Information: The Office of Financial Aid & Scholarships is seeking motivated, customer-focused students to join our Customer Service Team as a Peer Counselor I. This position provides an excellent opportunity to develop professional communication, customer service, problem-solving, and leadership skills while helping students and families navigate the financial aid process. Peer Counselors serve as a first point of contact for students, families, prospective students, and campus visitors seeking information about financial aid and university resources. Students in this role receive ongoing training and professional development while gaining valuable experience in higher education and student services. The Peer Counselor must be available to work up to 10 hours per week during office hours, Monday through Friday, between 8:00 a.m. and 5:00 p.m. Opportunities for summer employment may also be available. Duties and Responsibilities: ● Serve as a first point of contact for students, families, prospective students, and campus visitors seeking assistance with financial aid processes and services. ● Provide accurate, professional, and courteous information regarding financial aid applications, deadlines, documentation requirements, awards, and university resources. ● Respond to phone, email, and in-person inquiries while maintaining excellent customer service. ● Assist with monitoring and responding to the Office of Financial Aid & Scholarships general email inbox under staff guidance. ● Exercise sound judgment and appropriately refer complex questions to financial aid counselors, office staff, and other university departments. ● Maintain working knowledge of federal, state, institutional, and private financial aid programs, eligibility requirements, and application procedures. ● Develop proficiency with university systems and software, including PeopleSoft, Microsoft Office Suite, Windows operating systems, and other assigned technologies. ● Participate in orientation, required trainings, staff meetings, and professional development opportunities. ● Meet with staff members across the Office of Financial Aid & Scholarships to gain a broad understanding of departmental operations and services. ● Complete regular self-evaluations, weekly reflection journals, and scheduled check-ins with supervisors to support professional growth and development. ● Provide administrative support, data entry, record maintenance, document processing, and other office support functions as customer traffic permits. ● Assist with special projects and additional duties as assigned. ● Maintain confidentiality of student records and sensitive information in accordance with FERPA, university policies, and departmental procedures. ● Demonstrate professionalism, dependability, integrity, ethical conduct, and a commitment to creating a welcoming, inclusive, and student-centered environment. ● Accurately complete and submit timesheets by established deadlines and comply with all Student Employment policies. Qualifications: ● Excellent interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills. ● Strong customer service orientation and desire to help others. ● Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team. ● Strong attention to detail and organizational skills. ● Ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain professionalism when working with confidential information. ● Willingness to learn financial aid policies, procedures, and university resources. ● Ability to use Microsoft Office applications and learn university software systems. ● Dependable, responsible, and committed to meeting work expectations and deadlines. ● Available to work up to 10 hours per week during office hours, with potential opportunities for summer employment. Additional Posting Information: Students in this position will develop valuable career-readiness skills, including: ● Professional communication ● Customer service ● Teamwork and collaboration ● Critical thinking and problem-solving ● Technology proficiency ● Professionalism and workplace accountability ● Ethical decision-making and confidentiality ● Career and self-development This position provides meaningful work experience that supports future academic, professional, and career goals. Conditions of Employment: You must be a current JMU student (enrolled in at least 6 credits) who qualifies for Federal Work Study. Verification of FWS eligibility must be provided with your application. You can log on to your MyMadison and under Finances click ‘View My Financial Aid.’ Click on the current Aid Year. Copy and paste your award information into a Word document, and save. This document must be sent electronically along with your application when applying for FWS jobs. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are a student with a disability and need assistance please contact the Office of Disability Services at (540) 568-6705 or disability-svcs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the Office of Disability Services, located in the Student Success Center, Suite 1202 and they will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Know someone who would be interested in this job? First Name (required) 8cb80c8d Last Name (required) d4704b24 Email (required) e38105c4 Who would you like to send this job to? 7a3978f0 Refer Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recently Posted Jobs Associate Director, Research and Public Health 20002267 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) The Institute for Innovation in Health and Human Services (IIHHS) is accepting applications for a full-time Associate Director of Research and Public Health.\n\nThe Associate Director serves on the IIHHS Leadership Team, and takes a lead role in IIHHS strategic initiatives related to research and evaluation. This position also supervises and contributes to public health evaluation efforts done in partnership with the State, and is responsible for collaborating on grants to continue the public health research activities conducted out of IIHHS. This position also assists in grant applications to continue and grow our work across the Institute, and particularly in the areas of Research and Public Health. This role includes mentoring faculty and students as collaborators on research projects, and supports in-house evaluation efforts to build program capacity for evaluation. The Associate Director is a thought partner for and leads efforts to document social impact of IIHHS. The Associate Director supports the annual reporting efforts of IIHHS, including helping to strengthen and disseminate the annual report survey, preparing the data for the Director to include in the written annual report, and supporting data visualization efforts.\n\nIIHHS is seeking a creative, self-starting team member, who is effective working alone and as part of a team. The Associate Director supervises and works collaboratively with the PT Operations Coordinator, and also works collaboratively with colleagues across the Institute. The Associate Director ensures that all fiscal and personnel functions of the department operate at optimum efficiency, that grant funding supports program operations, and that deliverables stay on schedule and within budget. The Associate Director reports to the Director of IIHHS and provides fiscal and administrative support for areas and positions within the department.\n\nThis is not a remote/telework position. Student Case Administrator - Restorative Practices - IE 20002325 Student Employment Institutional Employment Student Case Administrators (SCAs) are undergraduate students who conduct one-on-one Individual Accountability Case Reviews for students who are alleged to have violated university policy. In Individual Accountability Case Reviews, SCAs evaluate evidence to determine whether or not the Responding Party is responsible for violating policy and, if applicable, assign outcomes. Student Case Administrators are undergraduate staff members in the Office of Student Accountability and Restorative Practices who participate in staff training and professional development; assist with various programs, outreach opportunities, and educational programs; and collaborate in the recruitment and selection of staff and volunteers. Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director 20002311 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty The Department of Health Professions in the College of Health and Behavioral Studies (CHBS) at James Madison University invites applications for Graduate Program Director of the Physician Assistant Studies program at the rank of Associate or Full Professor of Practice. This is a renewable term appointment. Accredited by ARC-PA, the program boasts a 98% first-time PANCE pass rate over the past five years and is supported by a stable, experienced faculty. The position offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across Health Professions programs and throughout the College. The preferred start date is January 1, 2027, with some flexibility based on candidate availability and institutional needs.\n\nThe successful candidate will join an engaged faculty at one of the nation's leading public universities. CHBS is committed to fostering a welcoming, innovative environment that supports individual and collective growth through education, scholarship, and service. Learn more about CHBS at https://www.jmu.edu/chbs/about.shtml Apply Now First Name (required) 5093ba2f Last Name (required) 35427e15 Email (required) 7c2bacd9 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Privacy Policy Quick Links Accessibility at JMU Application Instructions Notice of Availability - Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Perm Notices Student Employment Employment Posters © 2026 JAMES MADISON UNIVERSITY Before You Go.. Would You Like To Sign Up For Job Alerts? First Name (required) 658935e4 Last Name (required) f5aad00d Email (required) 44463d32 Job Alert fba07a7e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Employment Student Employment Employment Type Federal Work Study Federal Work Study Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
