    "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/assistant-director-of-global-and-international-research-engagement-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Global and International Research Engagement",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Global and International Research Engagement - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Home Explore JMU Benefits Navigate JMU Job Search My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode Assistant Director of Global and International Research Engagement 20002131 Vice President - REDI Research Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) Opening on: Sep 22 2026 Research, Economic Development and Innovation 539416 - Research Development IDC Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: Assistant Director of Global and International Research Engagement State Role Title: N/A Position Type: Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) Position Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Exempt: Not Eligible for Overtime College/Division: Vice President - REDI Department: 539416 - Research Development IDC Pay Band: N/A Pay Rate: Commensurate with Experience Specify Range or Amount: Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? Yes. This is a grant-funded position and is contingent upon continued funding. Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? No Beginning Review Date: 10/23/2026 About JMU: Mission We are a community committed to preparing students to be educated and enlightened citizens who lead productive and meaningful lives. Vision To be the national model for the engaged university: engaged with ideas and the world. Who We Are Situated in the heart of Virginia’s beautiful Shenandoah Valley, the city of Harrisonburg is a vibrant community with a population of approximately 52,000. Harrisonburg is conveniently located approximately 120 miles from Washington, D.C. and Richmond, VA. JMU is a selective, public institution with a growing national reputation for offering experiences that lead to an outstanding education and supportive environment for students, faculty and staff. The student body includes approximately 21,000 undergraduate and 1,800 graduate students, with over 1,000 full-time instructional faculty. JMU offers thriving programs in the liberal arts, science and technology, and professional disciplines at the undergraduate, master’s and doctoral levels. JMU has achieved national recognition for the high quality of its academic programs, focus on maintaining strong student/faculty interaction, and innovative faculty research. General Information: The Assistant Director of Global and International Research Engagement provides strategic leadership to advance James Madison University’s global research presence in alignment with its mission as a public, student‑centered R2 institution. The Assistant Director strengthens the university’s role as an engaged global knowledge partner by supporting intentional, ethical, and mission‑aligned international research collaborations that enhance faculty scholarship, expand societal impact, and elevate institutional reputation. This position focuses on building sustainable international research capacity at JMU—prioritizing faculty success, interdisciplinary collaboration, and strategic partnerships that complement the university’s emphasis on applied research, community engagement, and student involvement. The Assistant Director integrates global research engagement into JMU’s broader research development and competitiveness strategies, supporting both established and emerging scholars across disciplines. Duties and Responsibilities: Duties include: • Identify, analyze, and promote international and multinational external research funding opportunities aligned with James Madison University’s research priorities. • Advise faculty and interdisciplinary research teams on sponsor alignment, proposal positioning, and competitiveness in international funding contexts. • Support the development of strong international funding concepts, narratives, and collaboration models appropriate to JMU’s R2 profile. • Facilitate connections between JMU faculty and international collaborators, co principal investigators, and consortia. • Coordinate with research development, grant administration, and other campus partners to align proposal development and submission strategies. • Strengthen institutional capacity for sustainable growth in international grant activity through strategic guidance and coordination. • Provide strategic vision and leadership for JMU’s global and international research engagement portfolio. • Develop and advance a coherent institutional approach to international research engagement aligned with JMU’s mission and R2 research profile. • Integrate global research engagement into broader institutional research development, competitiveness, and growth initiatives. • Advise senior research leadership on international research opportunities, trends, and institutional positioning. • Identify priority geographies, thematic areas, and partnership models that enhance JMU’s scholarly visibility and impact while remaining scalable and intentional. • Enable faculty participation in international research by coordinating services, guidance, and institutional resources. • Support faculty in initiating, developing, and sustaining international research projects and collaborations. • Advise on collaboration design, sustainability, and competitiveness in global research contexts. • Promote inclusive access to international research engagement for early career faculty and interdisciplinary teams. • Collaborate with research development staff, college leadership, and campus partners to align support structures with faculty needs and research goals. • Cultivate and steward selected international research partnerships aligned with JMU’s academic strengths and applied research priorities. • Facilitate collaborations with international universities, research institutes, governments, NGOs, and research organizations. • Strengthen institutional capacity to initiate, coordinate, and sustain international research partnerships. • Prioritize partnership depth, mutual benefit, and long term scholarly value over volume. • Collaborate with campus units involved in internationalization, community engagement, and economic development to ensure institutional alignment and coordination. • Ensure that all international research engagement activities are ethically grounded, transparent, and aligned with university policies and values. • Collaborate with relevant offices to support appropriate coordination and stewardship of international research activities and agreements. • Promote best practices for responsible global research engagement across faculty activities and partnerships. • Represent James Madison University as a credible, principled, and engaged global research partner in international networks, alliances, and consortia. Qualifications: Required Qualifications • Earned Masters degree in a relevant academic or professional field. • Demonstrated experience in international research engagement, global partnerships, research development, or related areas within higher education or research organizations. • Proven ability to work collaboratively with faculty across diverse disciplines in a student‑centered, teaching‑engaged research environment. • Strong understanding of research capacity‑building and strategic growth at an R2 public university. • Excellent interpersonal, communication, and cross‑cultural engagement skills. Preferred Qualifications • Terminal degree in a relevant academic or professional field. • Experience supporting international or multinational research funding proposals and collaborative projects. • Familiarity with applied research, community‑engaged scholarship, or interdisciplinary research development. • Demonstrated success building sustainable partnerships that balance scholarly ambition with institutional capacity. Additional Posting Information: JMU’s Dual Career and Community Resources Program is available for candidates that will be relocating to the area. For more information, please visit https://bit.ly/2OTF1NG. Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) ac6b72bd Last Name (required) 4c785433 Email (required) 93e67b00 Job Alert a38a3a0c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research Research Employment Type Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Know someone who would be interested in this job? First Name (required) d3e2bd57 Last Name (required) dc8e1d79 Email (required) ac6d5258 Who would you like to send this job to? e8c4c564 Refer Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recently Posted Jobs Associate Director, Research and Public Health 20002267 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) The Institute for Innovation in Health and Human Services (IIHHS) is accepting applications for a full-time Associate Director of Research and Public Health.\n\nThe Associate Director serves on the IIHHS Leadership Team, and takes a lead role in IIHHS strategic initiatives related to research and evaluation. This position also supervises and contributes to public health evaluation efforts done in partnership with the State, and is responsible for collaborating on grants to continue the public health research activities conducted out of IIHHS. This position also assists in grant applications to continue and grow our work across the Institute, and particularly in the areas of Research and Public Health. This role includes mentoring faculty and students as collaborators on research projects, and supports in-house evaluation efforts to build program capacity for evaluation. The Associate Director is a thought partner for and leads efforts to document social impact of IIHHS. The Associate Director supports the annual reporting efforts of IIHHS, including helping to strengthen and disseminate the annual report survey, preparing the data for the Director to include in the written annual report, and supporting data visualization efforts.\n\nIIHHS is seeking a creative, self-starting team member, who is effective working alone and as part of a team. The Associate Director supervises and works collaboratively with the PT Operations Coordinator, and also works collaboratively with colleagues across the Institute. The Associate Director ensures that all fiscal and personnel functions of the department operate at optimum efficiency, that grant funding supports program operations, and that deliverables stay on schedule and within budget. The Associate Director reports to the Director of IIHHS and provides fiscal and administrative support for areas and positions within the department.\n\nThis is not a remote/telework position. Student Case Administrator - Restorative Practices - IE 20002325 Student Employment Institutional Employment Student Case Administrators (SCAs) are undergraduate students who conduct one-on-one Individual Accountability Case Reviews for students who are alleged to have violated university policy. In Individual Accountability Case Reviews, SCAs evaluate evidence to determine whether or not the Responding Party is responsible for violating policy and, if applicable, assign outcomes. Student Case Administrators are undergraduate staff members in the Office of Student Accountability and Restorative Practices who participate in staff training and professional development; assist with various programs, outreach opportunities, and educational programs; and collaborate in the recruitment and selection of staff and volunteers. Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director 20002311 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty The Department of Health Professions in the College of Health and Behavioral Studies (CHBS) at James Madison University invites applications for Graduate Program Director of the Physician Assistant Studies program at the rank of Associate or Full Professor of Practice. This is a renewable term appointment. Accredited by ARC-PA, the program boasts a 98% first-time PANCE pass rate over the past five years and is supported by a stable, experienced faculty. The position offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across Health Professions programs and throughout the College. The preferred start date is January 1, 2027, with some flexibility based on candidate availability and institutional needs.\n\nThe successful candidate will join an engaged faculty at one of the nation's leading public universities. CHBS is committed to fostering a welcoming, innovative environment that supports individual and collective growth through education, scholarship, and service. Learn more about CHBS at https://www.jmu.edu/chbs/about.shtml Apply Now First Name (required) 3a962ab4 Last Name (required) ccfc1e54 Email (required) fcb2901c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Privacy Policy Quick Links Accessibility at JMU Application Instructions Notice of Availability - Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Perm Notices Student Employment Employment Posters © 2026 JAMES MADISON UNIVERSITY Before You Go.. Would You Like To Sign Up For Job Alerts? First Name (required) d0954ece Last Name (required) 47e7f94a Email (required) fc481b4c Job Alert 2f2875ea Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research Research Employment Type Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operat