    "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/urec-facilities-manager-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states-13b1cd70-8fbb-4d6e-b1a8-5e8067ce779a": {
      "title": "UREC Facilities Manager",
      "description": "UREC Facilities Manager - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Home Explore JMU Benefits Navigate JMU Job Search My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode UREC Facilities Manager 20002299 Health and Wellbeing Recreation Center Full-time Staff (Classified) Opening on: Sep 21 2026 Student Affairs 300034 - University Recreation (UREC) Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: UREC Facilities Manager State Role Title: Trades Technician III Position Type: Full-time Staff (Classified) Position Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt: Eligible for Overtime College/Division: Health and Wellbeing Department: 300034 - University Recreation (UREC) Pay Band: 3 Pay Rate: Pay Range Specify Range or Amount: $48,000 - $53,000 Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? No Beginning Review Date: 09/29/2026 About JMU: At James Madison University (JMU), we’re more than just a publicly funded institution — we’re a vibrant, welcoming community located on a stunning campus where innovation, collaboration, and personal growth thrive. Our mission is to prepare students for a bright future, and we believe that starts with supporting the people who make it all possible: our employees. Why Work at JMU? We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your professional journey and personal wellbeing: • Generous Leave: Enjoy paid vacation, sick leave, parental leave, community service leave, and 19 paid holidays annually. • Comprehensive Health Coverage: Access high-quality health insurance options that fit your needs. • Retirement Options: Plan for your future with retirement benefits through the Virginia Retirement System. • Employee Well-Being: Our Balanced Dukes program promotes wellness and work-life integration through resources, events, and support. • Tuition Waiver Program: Advance your education with our tuition waiver program for undergraduate and graduate courses taken at JMU. At JMU, we believe in Being the Change — and that starts with creating an environment where you can grow, contribute meaningfully, and feel supported every step of the way. Discover what makes JMU a great place to work: bit.ly/JMUEmployment General Information: University Recreation (UREC) is currently seeking applicants for the Facilities Manager position. The Facilities Manager serves on the University Recreation (UREC) staff and reports to the Associate Director of Facilities & Operations. This position provides maintenance oversight for UREC's indoor and outdoor satellite facilities, ensuring safe, functional, and program-ready environments that support recreation programs, sport competitions, special events, and university engagement. UREC is a Health & Well-being department within the Student Affairs division. The mission of UREC is to promote and advance healthy lifestyles through educational programs, participation opportunities and supportive services. UREC’s qualified staff is committed to excellence and responsive to the developmental needs of their participants. UREC’s award-winning main facility is 278,515 square feet of recently expanded and renovated space. UREC looks for people who are passionate about teaching and working with students. Join us as we strive for excellence in building a welcoming atmosphere for every participant, visitor and employee! Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Satellite Facility Maintenance Perform weekly inspection, cleaning and minor repairs of all goals, fencing, netting, and site furnishings at satellite facilities (including but not limited to University Park, Team Challenge Course, Disc Golf Course, UREC trails, John Carr Field, Archery Range, UREC Turf, Long Mauck Stadium, Harper Allen Lee Studio, and Hillside Courts). Perform routine field maintenance on all UREC turf fields. Identify potential major maintenance needs for long term project planning. Provide equipment support to programs that utilize UPARK and Satellite Facilities. Coordinate equipment services to include shipping/receiving at UPARK and all satellite facilities. Performs weekly cleaning, trip prep (gas) and minor maintenance of small truck, all-terrain vehicles and electric golf cart. Maintain organized storage spaces at UPARK Bunker storage and Kelsey Lane facility. Ensure UPARK grill and propane tanks (UPARK & UREC) are cleaned, filled and ready for use by groups. Coordinate and inspect all satellite bathroom units (permanent and temporary) cleaned and supplied at least weekly, to ensure all housekeeping/service is performed to a high standard. 2. Shared Facility Maintenance Perform and plan the maintenance of shared satellite spaces in collaboration with space owner (including but not limited to Memorial Softball Practice Field, Godwin Combatives Room, Godwin Gymnastics Room, Godwin 135, and Field Hockey turf and track). Perform routine inspection and submit work orders to FM where appropriate and/or make Athletics staff aware of maintenance issues. Provide equipment support to programs that utilize shared facilities. Coordinates housekeeping to support special event programs in shared facilities. 3. Administration Prepares and tracks the overall budget for satellite facility maintenance and submits for approval according to UREC budget process deadlines. Initiates purchases for all satellite facility equipment and maintenance as needed. Utilizes Connect2Concepts software on a daily basis for all Satellite/Shared facility repairs identified by professional and student staff. Submits work orders via the FM AiM system for all work needing FM support. Conduct regular inspection of FM trades work orders to ensure completion according to UREC standards. Provides timely communication with all UREC staff in regards to ongoing facility and satellite facility projects that may affect programming. Reconciles all charge-back reports from FM to ensure accuracy and approves internal charges. Serves as the secondary Building Coordinator for UPARK and Satellite Facilities in the absence of the Associate Director for Facilities & Operations. 4. Collaboration Serves as a member of the UREC team and on committees as assigned. Attends departmental retreats, divisional meetings, bi-monthly departmental staff meetings, and 1-on-1 meetings with supervisor as scheduled. Attend UREC Event Operations meetings to ensure facilities are ready for UREC Sport Clubs, Intramural Sports, Special Events, general programming and reservations. Perform equipment repairs when Equipment Manager is out of office (priority repairs that have potential to be safety/risk management issue). Recruit, hire and train 1-2 student employees to support the overall satellite facility equipment and maintenance of UREC. Support opportunities for students to gain professional development Collaborate with UREC Equipment Manager on major equipment repairs as needed. On a periodic basis, adjust work schedule to support departmental major events. Qualifications: Required: Experience in facility maintenance Experience in equipment maintenance and repair Basic computer skills Valid Driver’s License Additional Considerations: Experience in outdoor sport and recreation facility maintenance (ex: line painting, turf grooming, natural grass maintenance, outdoor plumbing) Experience in outdoor/recreational equipment maintenance and repair (ex: scoreboards, sport goals) Experience independently overseeing internal and external contractors for maintenance and repair projects Experience driving/operating specialty outdoor vehicles/machinery (ex: turf groomer, turf field liner) Experience utilizing software programs relevant to position Ability to work collaboratively within a team and maintain strong relationships across the university and with vendors Additional Posting Information: Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) d6be1436 Last Name (required) 4b1837de Email (required) 1f940bd9 Job Alert 4b945f13 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Recreation Center Recreation Center Employment Type Full-time Staff (Classified) Full-time Staff (Classified) Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Know someone who would be interested in this job? First Name (required) 7043fffc Last Name (required) 9491f713 Email (required) 836c9cd0 Who would you like to send this job to? 2a7e9a57 Refer Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recently Posted Jobs Associate Director, Research and Public Health 20002267 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) The Institute for Innovation in Health and Human Services (IIHHS) is accepting applications for a full-time Associate Director of Research and Public Health.\n\nThe Associate Director serves on the IIHHS Leadership Team, and takes a lead role in IIHHS strategic initiatives related to research and evaluation. This position also supervises and contributes to public health evaluation efforts done in partnership with the State, and is responsible for collaborating on grants to continue the public health research activities conducted out of IIHHS. This position also assists in grant applications to continue and grow our work across the Institute, and particularly in the areas of Research and Public Health. This role includes mentoring faculty and students as collaborators on research projects, and supports in-house evaluation efforts to build program capacity for evaluation. The Associate Director is a thought partner for and leads efforts to document social impact of IIHHS. The Associate Director supports the annual reporting efforts of IIHHS, including helping to strengthen and disseminate the annual report survey, preparing the data for the Director to include in the written annual report, and supporting data visualization efforts.\n\nIIHHS is seeking a creative, self-starting team member, who is effective working alone and as part of a team. The Associate Director supervises and works collaboratively with the PT Operations Coordinator, and also works collaboratively with colleagues across the Institute. The Associate Director ensures that all fiscal and personnel functions of the department operate at optimum efficiency, that grant funding supports program operations, and that deliverables stay on schedule and within budget. The Associate Director reports to the Director of IIHHS and provides fiscal and administrative support for areas and positions within the department.\n\nThis is not a remote/telework position. Student Case Administrator - Restorative Practices - IE 20002325 Student Employment Institutional Employment Student Case Administrators (SCAs) are undergraduate students who conduct one-on-one Individual Accountability Case Reviews for students who are alleged to have violated university policy. In Individual Accountability Case Reviews, SCAs evaluate evidence to determine whether or not the Responding Party is responsible for violating policy and, if applicable, assign outcomes. Student Case Administrators are undergraduate staff members in the Office of Student Accountability and Restorative Practices who participate in staff training and professional development; assist with various programs, outreach opportunities, and educational programs; and collaborate in the recruitment and selection of staff and volunteers. Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director 20002311 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty The Department of Health Professions in the College of Health and Behavioral Studies (CHBS) at James Madison University invites applications for Graduate Program Director of the Physician Assistant Studies program at the rank of Associate or Full Professor of Practice. This is a renewable term appointment. Accredited by ARC-PA, the program boasts a 98% first-time PANCE pass rate over the past five years and is supported by a stable, experienced faculty. The position offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across Health Professions programs and throughout the College. The preferred start date is January 1, 2027, with some flexibility based on candidate availability and institutional needs.\n\nThe successful candidate will join an engaged faculty at one of the nation's leading public universities. CHBS is committed to fostering a welcoming, innovative environment that supports individual and collective growth through education, scholarship, and service. Learn more about CHBS at https://www.jmu.edu/chbs/about.shtml Apply Now First Name (required) a431c904 Last Name (required) fac031a4 Email (required) 4f0f161b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Privacy Policy Quick Links Accessibility at JMU Application Instructions Notice of Availability - Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Perm Notices Student Employment Employment Posters © 2026 JAMES MADISON UNIVERSITY Before You Go.. Would You Like To Sign Up For Job Alerts? First Name (required) 8d0ff437 Last Name (required) 2e57256c Email (required) 39ac57b4 Job Alert 9eadfb1c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Recreation Center Recreation Center Employment Type Full-time Staff (Classified) Full-time Staff (Classified) Locations Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
