    "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-school-of-media-arts-and-design-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - School of Media Arts and Design - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Home Explore JMU Benefits Navigate JMU Job Search My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode Assistant Professor - School of Media Arts and Design 20002292 College of Arts and Letters Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Opening on: Sep 21 2026 Academic Affairs 100018 - School of Media Arts Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: Assistant Professor - School of Media Arts and Design State Role Title: N/A Position Type: Instructional / Teaching Faculty Position Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Exempt: Not Eligible for Overtime College/Division: College of Arts and Letters Department: 100018 - School of Media Arts Pay Band: N/A Pay Rate: Commensurate with Experience Specify Range or Amount: Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? No Beginning Review Date: 10/22/2026 About JMU: Mission We are a community committed to preparing students to be educated and enlightened citizens who lead productive and meaningful lives. Vision To be the national model for the engaged university: engaged with ideas and the world. Who We Are Situated in the heart of Virginia’s beautiful Shenandoah Valley, the city of Harrisonburg is a vibrant community with a population of approximately 52,000. Harrisonburg is conveniently located approximately 120 miles from Washington, D.C. and Richmond, VA. JMU is a selective, public institution with a growing national reputation for offering experiences that lead to an outstanding education and supportive environment for students, faculty and staff. The student body includes approximately 21,000 undergraduate and 1,800 graduate students, with over 1,000 full-time instructional faculty. JMU offers thriving programs in the liberal arts, science and technology, and professional disciplines at the undergraduate, master’s and doctoral levels. JMU has achieved national recognition for the high quality of its academic programs, focus on maintaining strong student/faculty interaction, and innovative faculty research. General Information: The School of Media Arts and Design (SMAD) at James Madison University (JMU) invites applications for a tenure track appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor, beginning in August 2027. We seek a teacher-scholar whose instructional interests and research or creative practice engage visual communication, media literacy, mass media, audiences, storytelling, and culture. SMAD’s distinctive undergraduate major prepares students to become well-rounded multimedia storytellers and offers four concentrations: Creative Advertising, Digital Video and Cinema, Interactive Design, and Journalism. SMAD also boasts one of the nation’s finest media production facilities that offers instructional workspaces for creating video, audio, graphics, animation, websites, and apps. The school has about 700 undergraduate majors and more than 20 faculty members, who represent a blend of professional and academic interests. For more information, go to http://www.jmu.edu/smad. The School of Media Arts and Design is part of JMU’s College of Arts and Letters, which enrolls more than 3,100 undergraduate majors and about 150 graduate students across ten academic units. Home to several interdisciplinary centers and institutes, the College embraces the teacher-scholar model and encourages excellent applicants within our disciplines, as well as scholars and teachers eager to work across them. Duties and Responsibilities: SMAD seeks a student-focused colleague to teach a core course in visual literacy and culture, as well as some combination of foundations and critical analysis courses. Depending on the successful candidate’s experience, this position could also allow for teaching in one of SMAD’s four concentrations or in a media-centric General Education course. The teaching load is 3 courses each semester. Tenure-track faculty must have an active creative or scholarly agenda that may include juried production activity or peer-reviewed academic research. Tenure-track faculty also have service responsibilities and opportunities within the department, college, and institution. Qualifications: An MFA, Ph.D., or other terminal degree is required; ABD applicants with the degree near completion will be considered with the requirement that the terminal degree be conferred no later than August 2027. The preferred candidate will have college-level teaching as well as professional industry experience in media or related fields. Additional Posting Information: Interested candidates must complete the online application on the JMU career site and provide the following: -Cover letter -CV -Names and contact information for three references JMU’s Dual Career and Community Resources Program is available for candidates that will be relocating to the area. For more information, please visit https://bit.ly/2OTF1NG. Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Recently Posted Jobs Associate Director, Research and Public Health 20002267 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) The Institute for Innovation in Health and Human Services (IIHHS) is accepting applications for a full-time Associate Director of Research and Public Health.\n\nThe Associate Director serves on the IIHHS Leadership Team, and takes a lead role in IIHHS strategic initiatives related to research and evaluation. This position also supervises and contributes to public health evaluation efforts done in partnership with the State, and is responsible for collaborating on grants to continue the public health research activities conducted out of IIHHS. This position also assists in grant applications to continue and grow our work across the Institute, and particularly in the areas of Research and Public Health. This role includes mentoring faculty and students as collaborators on research projects, and supports in-house evaluation efforts to build program capacity for evaluation. The Associate Director is a thought partner for and leads efforts to document social impact of IIHHS. The Associate Director supports the annual reporting efforts of IIHHS, including helping to strengthen and disseminate the annual report survey, preparing the data for the Director to include in the written annual report, and supporting data visualization efforts.\n\nIIHHS is seeking a creative, self-starting team member, who is effective working alone and as part of a team. The Associate Director supervises and works collaboratively with the PT Operations Coordinator, and also works collaboratively with colleagues across the Institute. The Associate Director ensures that all fiscal and personnel functions of the department operate at optimum efficiency, that grant funding supports program operations, and that deliverables stay on schedule and within budget. The Associate Director reports to the Director of IIHHS and provides fiscal and administrative support for areas and positions within the department.\n\nThis is not a remote/telework position. Student Case Administrator - Restorative Practices - IE 20002325 Student Employment Institutional Employment Student Case Administrators (SCAs) are undergraduate students who conduct one-on-one Individual Accountability Case Reviews for students who are alleged to have violated university policy. In Individual Accountability Case Reviews, SCAs evaluate evidence to determine whether or not the Responding Party is responsible for violating policy and, if applicable, assign outcomes. Student Case Administrators are undergraduate staff members in the Office of Student Accountability and Restorative Practices who participate in staff training and professional development; assist with various programs, outreach opportunities, and educational programs; and collaborate in the recruitment and selection of staff and volunteers. Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director 20002311 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty The Department of Health Professions in the College of Health and Behavioral Studies (CHBS) at James Madison University invites applications for Graduate Program Director of the Physician Assistant Studies program at the rank of Associate or Full Professor of Practice. This is a renewable term appointment. Accredited by ARC-PA, the program boasts a 98% first-time PANCE pass rate over the past five years and is supported by a stable, experienced faculty. The position offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across Health Professions programs and throughout the College. The preferred start date is January 1, 2027, with some flexibility based on candidate availability and institutional needs.\n\nThe successful candidate will join an engaged faculty at one of the nation's leading public universities. CHBS is committed to fostering a welcoming, innovative environment that supports individual and collective growth through education, scholarship, and service. Learn more about CHBS at https://www.jmu.edu/chbs/about.shtml Privacy Policy Quick Links Accessibility at JMU Application Instructions Notice of Availability - Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Perm Notices Student Employment Employment Posters © 2026 JAMES MADISON UNIVERSITY Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/integrations-developer-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Integrations Developer",
      "description": "Integrations Developer - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Home Explore JMU Benefits Navigate JMU Job Search My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode Integrations Developer 20002304 Information Technology Information Technology Full-time Staff (Classified) Opening on: Sep 21 2026 Administration and Finance 100211 - Enterprise Applications Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: Integrations Developer State Role Title: Information Technology Specialist II Position Type: Full-time Staff (Classified) Position Status: Full-Time FLSA Status: Exempt: Not Eligible for Overtime College/Division: Information Technology Department: 100211 - Enterprise Applications Pay Band: 5 Pay Rate: Pay Range Specify Range or Amount: $70,000 - $75,000 Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? No Beginning Review Date: 9/29/2026 About JMU: At James Madison University (JMU), we’re more than just a publicly funded institution — we’re a vibrant, welcoming community located on a stunning campus where innovation, collaboration, and personal growth thrive. Our mission is to prepare students for a bright future, and we believe that starts with supporting the people who make it all possible: our employees. Why Work at JMU? We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your professional journey and personal wellbeing: • Generous Leave: Enjoy paid vacation, sick leave, parental leave, community service leave, and 19 paid holidays annually. • Comprehensive Health Coverage: Access high-quality health insurance options that fit your needs. • Retirement Options: Plan for your future with retirement benefits through the Virginia Retirement System. • Employee Well-Being: Our Balanced Dukes program promotes wellness and work-life integration through resources, events, and support. • Tuition Waiver Program: Advance your education with our tuition waiver program for undergraduate and graduate courses taken at JMU. At JMU, we believe in Being the Change — and that starts with creating an environment where you can grow, contribute meaningfully, and feel supported every step of the way. Discover what makes JMU a great place to work: bit.ly/JMUEmployment General Information: JMU is in the midst of implementing a very large strategic initiative, Reengineering Madison (https://www.jmu.edu/computing/projects/reengineering-madison/index.shtml). Replacing our Enterprise Resource Management (ERP) applications is the final phase of the project, and we are excited to offer this position for Integration Developer to support the University's Oracle HCM, Finance, and Student applications. Duties and Responsibilities: This position will serve as a technical resource for Enterprise Applications with a primary focus on integrations supporting Oracle HCM, Finance (ERP/EPM), and Student applications. The initial implementation phases will focus on Oracle HCM and Finance (ERP/EPM) with a planned go-live of Summer 2027. Responsibilities include designing, developing, implementing, monitoring, maintaining, and supporting integrations between Oracle Cloud applications and other university systems. The position will partner closely with business offices, technical teams, implementation partners, vendors, and other stakeholders to understand data exchange requirements and develop secure, scalable, and maintainable integration solutions. Responsibilities include gathering and analyzing requirements, developing and testing integrations, troubleshooting issues, optimizing performance, maintaining documentation, and providing ongoing operational support. The successful candidate will stay current with Oracle Cloud, Oracle Integration Cloud (OIC), API technologies, security best practices, and emerging integration capabilities to ensure the University continues to leverage modern and effective integration solutions. Knowledge and experience with Boomi and PeopleSoft Campus Solutions will be helpful as those integrations will continue to be maintained until that system is replaced. This position is eligible for a remote work schedule. Qualifications: Required: • Significant professional experience designing, developing, implementing, and supporting enterprise system integrations using Oracle Integration Cloud (OIC). • Professional experience with Oracle Cloud applications, including HCM, ERP, EPM, Financials, Payroll, Recruiting, or Student systems. • Demonstrated experience gathering business and technical requirements and translating those requirements into effective integration solutions. • Professional experience working with integration technologies, APIs, web services, data exchange processes, or middleware platforms. • Professional experience managing multiple priorities and projects simultaneously. • Demonstrated strong analytical, troubleshooting, and problem-solving skills. • Exceptional communication skills, both verbal and written. • Significant professional experience partnering with business users, technical staff, vendors, and stakeholders of varying technical backgrounds. • Demonstrated ability to learn new technologies and deliver effective technical solutions. Additional Considerations: • Experience in a Higher Education environment. • Experience with Boomi integration platform and/or PeopleSoft Campus Solutions. • Experience supporting complex enterprise application ecosystems. • Experience with integration architecture, security protocols, authentication methods, and data governance principles. • Experience building strong and long-lasting partnerships with key stakeholders. • Experience supporting system modernization, cloud migration, or enterprise transformation initiatives. Additional Posting Information: Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Recently Posted Jobs Associate Director, Research and Public Health 20002267 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) The Institute for Innovation in Health and Human Services (IIHHS) is accepting applications for a full-time Associate Director of Research and Public Health.\n\nThe Associate Director serves on the IIHHS Leadership Team, and takes a lead role in IIHHS strategic initiatives related to research and evaluation. This position also supervises and contributes to public health evaluation efforts done in partnership with the State, and is responsible for collaborating on grants to continue the public health research activities conducted out of IIHHS. This position also assists in grant applications to continue and grow our work across the Institute, and particularly in the areas of Research and Public Health. This role includes mentoring faculty and students as collaborators on research projects, and supports in-house evaluation efforts to build program capacity for evaluation. The Associate Director is a thought partner for and leads efforts to document social impact of IIHHS. The Associate Director supports the annual reporting efforts of IIHHS, including helping to strengthen and disseminate the annual report survey, preparing the data for the Director to include in the written annual report, and supporting data visualization efforts.\n\nIIHHS is seeking a creative, self-starting team member, who is effective working alone and as part of a team. The Associate Director supervises and works collaboratively with the PT Operations Coordinator, and also works collaboratively with colleagues across the Institute. The Associate Director ensures that all fiscal and personnel functions of the department operate at optimum efficiency, that grant funding supports program operations, and that deliverables stay on schedule and within budget. The Associate Director reports to the Director of IIHHS and provides fiscal and administrative support for areas and positions within the department.\n\nThis is not a remote/telework position. Student Case Administrator - Restorative Practices - IE 20002325 Student Employment Institutional Employment Student Case Administrators (SCAs) are undergraduate students who conduct one-on-one Individual Accountability Case Reviews for students who are alleged to have violated university policy. In Individual Accountability Case Reviews, SCAs evaluate evidence to determine whether or not the Responding Party is responsible for violating policy and, if applicable, assign outcomes. Student Case Administrators are undergraduate staff members in the Office of Student Accountability and Restorative Practices who participate in staff training and professional development; assist with various programs, outreach opportunities, and educational programs; and collaborate in the recruitment and selection of staff and volunteers. Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director 20002311 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty The Department of Health Professions in the College of Health and Behavioral Studies (CHBS) at James Madison University invites applications for Graduate Program Director of the Physician Assistant Studies program at the rank of Associate or Full Professor of Practice. This is a renewable term appointment. Accredited by ARC-PA, the program boasts a 98% first-time PANCE pass rate over the past five years and is supported by a stable, experienced faculty. The position offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across Health Professions programs and throughout the College. The preferred start date is January 1, 2027, with some flexibility based on candidate availability and institutional needs.\n\nThe successful candidate will join an engaged faculty at one of the nation's leading public universities. CHBS is committed to fostering a welcoming, innovative environment that supports individual and collective growth through education, scholarship, and service. Learn more about CHBS at https://www.jmu.edu/chbs/about.shtml Privacy Policy Quick Links Accessibility at JMU Application Instructions Notice of Availability - Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Perm Notices Student Employment Employment Posters © 2026 JAMES MADISON UNIVERSITY Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
