    "https://jobs.jmu.edu/jobs/office-assistant-office-of-the-registrar-part-time-harrisonburg-virginia-united-states-63e7a183-a6c7-49e0-aca0-70f2e0c4c93f": {
      "title": "Office Assistant",
      "description": "Office Assistant - Office of the Registrar (Part-Time) - Harrisonburg, Virginia, United States Home Explore JMU Benefits Navigate JMU Job Search My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode Office Assistant - Office of the Registrar (Part-Time) 20002300 Student Academic Success Administrative / Office Staff Part-time - Wage / Part-time Salaried Opening on: Sep 18 2026 Academic Affairs 100177 - Office Of The Registrar Add to favorites View favorites Working Title: Office Assistant - Office of the Registrar (Part-Time) State Role Title: Administrative and Office Specialist II Position Type: Part-time - Wage / Part-time Salaried Position Status: Part-Time FLSA Status: Non-Exempt: Eligible for Overtime College/Division: Student Academic Success Department: 100177 - Office Of The Registrar Pay Band: 2 Pay Rate: Hourly Specify Range or Amount: $17.05 Is this a JMU only position? No Is this a grant-funded position? No Is this a Conflict of Interest designated position? No Beginning Review Date: 09/28/2026 About JMU: At James Madison University (JMU), we’re more than just a publicly funded institution — we’re a vibrant, welcoming community located on a stunning campus where innovation, collaboration, and personal growth thrive. Our mission is to prepare students for a bright future, and we believe that starts with supporting the people who make it all possible: our employees. JMU offers several perks to all employees including: • A Tuition Waiver Program that allows employees to have tuition waived for undergraduate and graduate level courses taken at JMU. • Free Access to the University Recreation Center (UREC): Employees can enjoy facility access and program registration privileges at UREC and University Park. This includes the climbing wall, equipment centers, and group exercise studios. • A variety of voluntary benefits such as Pet Insurance, Identity Theft and Legal Protection Plans, and several other supplemental benefits. • Holiday Breaks: The university is granted 12 holidays a year. • Talent Development Trainings: The Talent Development department offers a wide variety of personal and professional trainings, eligible for all employees to join. At JMU, we believe in Being the Change — and that starts with creating an environment where you can grow, contribute meaningfully, and feel supported every step of the way. Discover what makes JMU a great place to work: bit.ly/JMUEmployment General Information: The Office of the Registrar at James Madison University is accepting applications for a part-time Office Assistant. This position will serve a vital role with the Client Services Team in the Office of the Registrar. We are recruiting for one part-time wage position. The position will be a year-round, part-time position with no benefits, working an average of 29 hours per week (1,500 hours a year) over the course of a calendar year. Duties and Responsibilities: • Assist with answering phones, emails, and providing customer service coverage to our front desk • Process transcript orders and assist current and former students with placing transcript orders • Enter data into the PeopleSoft Student Administration System while ensuring data integrity, confidentiality, and accuracy • Scanning documents into OnBase (document retention system) • Work closely with students, faculty, staff, and parents/families • Performs back-up duties for other team members as needed • Performs other duties as assigned by supervisor, or designee Qualifications: Required: • Must have prior customer service experience, including phone, email, and in-person • Proficient in Microsoft Word and Microsoft Excel • Must have exceptional attention to detail and accuracy in work • Excellent organizational skills, ability to prioritize work, and multitask • Experience with working independently and within a team Additional Considerations: • Knowledge of PeopleSoft Student Administration System • Knowledge or experience with FERPA (Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act) Additional Posting Information: Conditions of Employment: Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of a criminal background check. This is a part-time wage position working up to an average of 29 hours per week over the course of a calendar year with no benefits. E-Verify Notice: After accepting employment, new hires are required to complete an I-9 form and present documentation of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. James Madison University uses the E-Verify system to confirm identity and work authorization. EEO Statement: James Madison University is committed to creating and supporting a diverse and inclusive work and educational community that is free of all forms of discrimination. This institution does not tolerate discrimination or harassment on the basis of age, color, disability, gender identity or expression, genetic information, national origin, parental status, political affiliation, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation or veteran status. We promote access, inclusion and diversity for all students, faculty, staff, constituents and programs, believing that these qualities are foundational components of an outstanding education in keeping with our mission. The university is interested in candidates whose experience and qualifications support an ongoing commitment to this core quality. Anyone having questions concerning discrimination should contact the Office for Equal Opportunity: (540) 568-6991. Reasonable Accommodation: If you are an individual with a disability and need assistance searching or applying for jobs please contact us at (540) 568-3597 or jobs@jmu.edu. You may also visit the JMU Human Resource Office, located at 752 Ott Street, Harrisonburg, VA 22807 and we will be happy to assist you. Apply Now Total Compensation Estimator Recently Posted Jobs Associate Director, Research and Public Health 20002267 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Administrative & Professional (Non-teaching Faculty) The Institute for Innovation in Health and Human Services (IIHHS) is accepting applications for a full-time Associate Director of Research and Public Health.\n\nThe Associate Director serves on the IIHHS Leadership Team, and takes a lead role in IIHHS strategic initiatives related to research and evaluation. This position also supervises and contributes to public health evaluation efforts done in partnership with the State, and is responsible for collaborating on grants to continue the public health research activities conducted out of IIHHS. This position also assists in grant applications to continue and grow our work across the Institute, and particularly in the areas of Research and Public Health. This role includes mentoring faculty and students as collaborators on research projects, and supports in-house evaluation efforts to build program capacity for evaluation. The Associate Director is a thought partner for and leads efforts to document social impact of IIHHS. The Associate Director supports the annual reporting efforts of IIHHS, including helping to strengthen and disseminate the annual report survey, preparing the data for the Director to include in the written annual report, and supporting data visualization efforts.\n\nIIHHS is seeking a creative, self-starting team member, who is effective working alone and as part of a team. The Associate Director supervises and works collaboratively with the PT Operations Coordinator, and also works collaboratively with colleagues across the Institute. The Associate Director ensures that all fiscal and personnel functions of the department operate at optimum efficiency, that grant funding supports program operations, and that deliverables stay on schedule and within budget. The Associate Director reports to the Director of IIHHS and provides fiscal and administrative support for areas and positions within the department.\n\nThis is not a remote/telework position. Student Case Administrator - Restorative Practices - IE 20002325 Student Employment Institutional Employment Student Case Administrators (SCAs) are undergraduate students who conduct one-on-one Individual Accountability Case Reviews for students who are alleged to have violated university policy. In Individual Accountability Case Reviews, SCAs evaluate evidence to determine whether or not the Responding Party is responsible for violating policy and, if applicable, assign outcomes. Student Case Administrators are undergraduate staff members in the Office of Student Accountability and Restorative Practices who participate in staff training and professional development; assist with various programs, outreach opportunities, and educational programs; and collaborate in the recruitment and selection of staff and volunteers. Physician Assistant Studies Graduate Program Director 20002311 Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty The Department of Health Professions in the College of Health and Behavioral Studies (CHBS) at James Madison University invites applications for Graduate Program Director of the Physician Assistant Studies program at the rank of Associate or Full Professor of Practice. This is a renewable term appointment. Accredited by ARC-PA, the program boasts a 98% first-time PANCE pass rate over the past five years and is supported by a stable, experienced faculty. The position offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across Health Professions programs and throughout the College. The preferred start date is January 1, 2027, with some flexibility based on candidate availability and institutional needs.\n\nThe successful candidate will join an engaged faculty at one of the nation's leading public universities. CHBS is committed to fostering a welcoming, innovative environment that supports individual and collective growth through education, scholarship, and service. Learn more about CHBS at https://www.jmu.edu/chbs/about.shtml Privacy Policy Quick Links Accessibility at JMU Application Instructions Notice of Availability - Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Perm Notices Student Employment Employment Posters © 2026 JAMES MADISON UNIVERSITY Close Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalize, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
